t</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 03-04-2016, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T01:38:49-08:00","id":844974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=842130#post842130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I've got a small contribution, but it may be helpful for those of us who are historically minded. Dreams of Avarice prompted me to review Sothis Ascends to try and chronicle of the reign of Unas in CofD. I had to make some educated guess, but I was able to do some with the help of historical chronicles.<br /> <br /> For those of you who are visually inclined (I know I am) there is a timeline in the spoiler below. If you are having trouble reading it, open it in its own tab to make it bigger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify. Does Awakened Diaspora happen to refer to <i>actual</i> Mages? Because if it does, I might explore that when I got the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T11:05:27-08:00","id":845727,"title":"","content":"I <i>think</i> Second Chances meant to write &quot;Arisen Diaspora&quot; there. This was the period when the Diasporic Code was written by the Sesha-Hebsu, headed specifically by one of the canon characters- the Prince of Glass (don't have the book with me at the moment for his <i>actual</i> name).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T11:59:40-08:00","id":845756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=845727#post845727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>think</i> Second Chances meant to write &quot;Arisen Diaspora&quot; there. This was the period when the Diasporic Code was written by the Sesha-Hebsu, headed specifically by one of the canon characters- the Prince of Glass (don't have the book with me at the moment for his <i>actual</i> name).</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoops! My bad. Yes, that's what I meant, I'll go fix that. I'll see if I can't comb Guildhalls this weekend in between creating exams and get a bit more context on the era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T12:21:22-08:00","id":845766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=845756#post845756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whoops! My bad. Yes, that's what I meant, I'll go fix that. I'll see if I can't comb Guildhalls this weekend in between creating exams and get a bit more context on the era.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take your time. The more Mummy material sifted through for easy perusal. the better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T18:21:49-07:00","id":847950,"title":"","content":"This is all great stuff. If I ever do a First Sothic Turn game I'll be using all of this, except one point where I quibble on the vampire clans:<br /> <br /> The Mumviri? I cringed when I saw they had Vigor and Stamina instead of Resilience and Resolve, especially once you had them gain the Ventrue Clan Bane if they get embraced in a non-traditional way. It just threw off the otherwise entertaining and perfect fit there for me. Part of that is just how I view the five clans as universals, and the Julii as strictly a cultural variation on the Ventrue, so that might just be me. <br /> <br /> I'm not saying it's objectively bad, it just gets up in my craw for entirely subjective reasons like above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T18:43:13-07:00","id":847955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=847950#post847950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is all great stuff. If I ever do a First Sothic Turn game I'll be using all of this, except one point where I quibble on the vampire clans:<br /> <br /> The Mumviri? I cringed when I saw they had Vigor and Stamina instead of Resilience and Resolve, especially once you had them gain the Ventrue Clan Bane if they get embraced in a non-traditional way. It just threw off the otherwise entertaining and perfect fit there for me. Part of that is just how I view the five clans as universals, and the Julii as strictly a cultural variation on the Ventrue, so that might just be me. <br /> <br /> I'm not saying it's objectively bad, it just gets up in my craw for entirely subjective reasons like above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you like it.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> And if ever you have ideas you want to add, feel free to do so.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I think I get what you're trying to say on the Mumvuri. And it <i>does</i> seem like an odd disconnect that the more 'conventional' Embrace only gives them the Ventrue Bane. Maybe it could be revised that the Clan Attributes and Disciplines are altered somewhat with the absence of a Shiri.<br /> <br /> Either way, the Lightning Birds were conceptualized as being a Clan that predated (but are similar to) the Ventrue, as the Lords don't fit in this particular era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T18:52:44-07:00","id":847959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=828208#post828208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This looks fascinating. I'll be watching this.<br /> <br /> Also, if you need anything on Sin-Eaters or the Underworld, I've got some ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in-between working on my Changeling 2E Homebrew, Beast (and Hero) homebrew, and two minor templates (one original, and the other a conversion of Inferno's Seventh Generation), I'm trying to figure out two things Age of Azar-related.<br /> <br /> a) Benefits for a Mystery Cult Initiation [Cult of Nekhbet] (go further up the thread for the incomplete draft I have on it)<br /> b) Sin-Eaters in the Black Land<br /> <br /> Seeing as you offered up ideas, how do you imagine the Bound being organized in that era?<br /> <br /> Arcanist, LostLight, and I (not sure which of us pitched it at first) mentioned how they might form the core group on the Cult of Anpu/Anubis, but it's pretty safe to say that they might also be common among other Cults, especially that of Nebthet (the Silent Temple).<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, I am thinking of putting up a link to my GDoc for the Mummy House Rules here (and in my homebrew hub) soon. Stay tuned.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 03-15-2016, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T20:10:42-07:00","id":847977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=847955#post847955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Glad you like it.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> And if ever you have ideas you want to add, feel free to do so.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I think I get what you're trying to say on the Mumvuri. And it <i>does</i> seem like an odd disconnect that the more 'conventional' Embrace only gives them the Ventrue Bane. Maybe it could be revised that the Clan Attributes and Disciplines are altered somewhat with the absence of a Shiri.<br /> <br /> Either way, the Lightning Birds were conceptualized as being a Clan that predated (but are similar to) the Ventrue, as the Lords don't fit in this particular era.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see what you mean. Still, if I ever use the material myself I'll be editing it so Mumvuri have Resilience and Resolve like the Ventrue and Julii instead.<br /> <br /> On a different note, I'm rather curious to see how the utterly amnesiac Deathless will react to all these hungry Lifeless lurking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T20:20:43-07:00","id":847981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=847977#post847977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a different note, I'm rather curious to see how the utterly amnesiac Deathless will react to all these hungry Lifeless lurking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>If by hungry Lifeless, you mean Kindred, then that's up in the air and dependent on individual Arisen. If it's <i>actual</i> Lifeless, though... Well, they're definitely in trouble. Especially once Apep is thrown in the mix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T20:49:52-07:00","id":847988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=847981#post847981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If by hungry Lifeless, you mean Kindred, then that's up in the air and dependent on individual Arisen. If it's <i>actual</i> Lifeless, though... Well, they're definitely in trouble. Especially once Apep is thrown in the mix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kindred are definitely Lifeless. They just have no particular reason to munch on Relics or Arisen, so they don't draw as much attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T21:29:43-07:00","id":848003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=847988#post847988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kindred are definitely Lifeless. They just have no particular reason to munch on Relics or Arisen, so they don't draw as much attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they <i>still</i> might take offense at the Hungry Dead exploiting relics like pesky mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T09:27:58-07:00","id":848222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=847959#post847959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So in-between working on my Changeling 2E Homebrew, Beast (and Hero) homebrew, and two minor templates (one original, and the other a conversion of Inferno's Seventh Generation), I'm trying to figure out two things Age of Azar-related.<br /> <br /> a) Benefits for a Mystery Cult Initiation [Cult of Nekhbet] (go further up the thread for the incomplete draft I have on it)<br /> b) Sin-Eaters in the Black Land<br /> <br /> Seeing as you offered up ideas, how do you imagine the Bound being organized in that era?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I see a few different options for S-E organization at the time:<br /> <br /> 1. Sin-Eaters integrated into mortal priesthoods. This is probably most prevalent among those whose geists take on aspects of contemporary divinities. The myth of Osiris probably resonates strongly with many of the Bound.<br /> <br /> 2. Sin-Eaters have their own cults away from mortal religious institutions, to protect the true secrets of the Great Below. They are probably also at least partly influenced by some remnants of Lost Irem. It's also possible the Rite of Return wrecked the local Underworld for centuries, and Sin-Eaters are still dealing with the fallout.<br /> <br /> 3. Sin-Eaters stick to themselves and don't organize. Either it's because having a ghost in your head is not particularly emotionally healthy, or because there's a general stigma attached to the Bound (mortal or supernatural, or a bit of both). The Underworld doesn't really mesh right with mortal religions, Arisen cults won't take them, and Egypt at the time is crawling with necromantic problems. Many Sin-Eaters tend to be wanderer-in-the-wilderness types, stalking the dunes and alleyways as weird shamans.<br /> <br /> Any of these, or all three even, could exist in concurrence.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T12:55:06-07:00","id":848356,"title":"","content":"Glad you like it Aiden. As I recall, we ended up deciding on the change with the Mumvuri explicitly so they wouldn't be just 'not-Ventrue' but I can see where that could go wrong.<br /> <br /> Espritdecalamar, all of your options sound extremely appealing, but especially the second and third ones. I'll be sure to take them into account when we get around to Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> A little extra detail on the setting, including some highly speculative math on the supernatural population of First Turn Kemet.<br /> <br /> <b>Ancient Egyptian Population: </b>2 000 000<br /> <br /> <b>Mummy Population:</b> 9 250<ul><li><b>Deceived:</b> 294</li> <li><b>Arisen:</b> 6 717 - 7 350<ul><li>If the Shan'iatu made the Arisen in batches of 42, and there are 35 Shan'iatu other than the Deceived temakh, then each Shan'iatu made roughly 198 Arisen, which divided by 42 comes out to 4.7, and if we round that up to five (one batch per Pillar), then we come to the tidier number of about 210 Arisen per Shan'iatu.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Shuankhsen:</b> 1 615 - 2 248</li> </ul><b>Supernatural Population Approx. 0.5%</b> <b>of Total</b><b>: </b>10 000<br /> <b>(1:10 Major Templates to associated mortals, 1:3 Major Templates to Minor Templates): </b>9000 Minor, 1000 Major<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire Population (1:10 000 in Urban Environments): </b>200<ul><li><b>Ghouls: </b>600</li> <li><b>Clans</b><ul><li><b>\u200bMekhet:</b> 80</li> <li><b>Ushabti: </b>60</li> <li><b>Habiru: </b>40</li> <li><b>Daeva: </b>20</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Mortals &quot;In the Know&quot;/Other Vampire Weirdness: </b>1200</li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> *****<br /> <br /> And now, a little fluff on how the Kindred of Kemet see the Strix.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>We are the damned, existing in defiance of Ma'at, persisting only to avoid falling into the jaws of Ammut. We are without </i>Ka <i>and so we take it from others, we are torn from Duat and so we leave behind our </i>Ba <i>and our </i>Sheut. <i>In time, both will come back to haunt us. Left without </i>Ka, <i>there is nothing in our souls for the </i>Ba<i>, our spirit, ambition, our drive to act, to latch onto. In time, we decay, becoming little more than ravenous corpses. We remember our </i>Ba <i>because we must, in order to survive until it can return to us- but it does not return to us pleased. Abandoned in Duat, sustained only by the paltry power of the </i>Sheut <i>our </i>Bas <i>return with wrath, seeking retribution, seeking vengeance. They are winged shadows with wrathful yellow eyes, testing our worthiness, seeking only to prove to us what we have become, what we reduced all that was once us into. Every single one of the Hungry Dead has their </i>Ba <i>waiting for them, twisted by the Slaughterers of Duat and infected by the twisted reflection of the </i>Sheut<i>, they are as devoid of </i>Ka <i>as we are, consumed by the same perverse desires, unrestrained by the guidance of </i>Ab <i>and </i>Ren.<br /> <br /> <i>They come for us all, in time. All except for the Khaibit, who have made their peace with Duat. But the rest of us? We, trembling, fear the passage of wings and the screech owl's cry.</i></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T13:47:42-07:00","id":848391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=847950#post847950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is all great stuff. If I ever do a First Sothic Turn game I'll be using all of this, except one point where I quibble on the vampire clans:<br /> <br /> The Mumviri? I cringed when I saw they had Vigor and Stamina instead of Resilience and Resolve, especially once you had them gain the Ventrue Clan Bane if they get embraced in a non-traditional way. It just threw off the otherwise entertaining and perfect fit there for me. Part of that is just how I view the five clans as universals, and the Julii as strictly a cultural variation on the Ventrue, so that might just be me.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it's objectively bad, it just gets up in my craw for entirely subjective reasons like above.</div> </div> </div> </div>as the one to make those decisions about the Mumviri, I think I should explain my reasons for those choices- like Arcanist have said, when designing the Clan, I didn't wished for them to be just &quot;another Ventrue&quot;. With 2E and Wicked Dead's attitude toward Clans as the &quot;most successful breeds of vampires&quot; instead of universal archetypes, that felt for me as the better path to go with. Also, unlike the Gangrel and the Nosferatu (who don't feel too tied toward a certain region), or the Daeva and the Mekhet (who have an origin tied to the regions covered by the Era), the Ventrue are strongly tied to the Western Culture, and with the Ventrue's representation as the most &quot;modern&quot; Clan which may or may not be connected to the Gangrel, I've felt it may harm the Vantrue's themes more than help. Thee was also another more &quot;petty&quot; reason, in which I wanted to do a shout out to the Lasombra from Masquerade, with the Shiri being used as their &quot;shadow power&quot;.<br /> <br /> And while including all of that, I've still wanted to keep a possible tie to them as the future Ventrue- which is why I've made it so when they use the conventional Embrace, they suffer from the Ventrue's bane. That should make you ask some questions- like, are the Mumvuri and the Ventrue trully two different Clans? If the vampires of ancient Punt truly are the foresires of the modern Lords, than why did they changed? Perhaps there was some sort of war between them and the Gangrel, resulting with the modern version? Maybe it was some change in the blood, as certain bloodline grew in power and consumed it from the inside- and maybe that bloodline's name was the Julii? Maybe it is just a matter of evolution- the Mumvuri were the primal kings of old age, but as times changed so did how one viewed kingship, and with that the clan itself changed into a more &quot;tamed&quot; version as we know in modern times. If that's the case, then may other Clans could be changed as well- and maybe the have been changed through history, again and again and again. And if the change in disciplines is independant from the change in the Clan's Bane, than what stops a modern Ventrue from Embracing using a strix, as they did in the old days?<br /> <br /> Still, on your table, you can do what ever works better for your games- and this is homebrew, after all. You should feel free to scavenge what you like and change what you don't <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T15:30:26-07:00","id":848441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=848222#post848222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I see a few different options for S-E organization at the time:<br /> <br /> 1. Sin-Eaters integrated into mortal priesthoods. This is probably most prevalent among those whose geists take on aspects of contemporary divinities. The myth of Osiris probably resonates strongly with many of the Bound.<br /> <br /> 2. Sin-Eaters have their own cults away from mortal religious institutions, to protect the true secrets of the Great Below. They are probably also at least partly influenced by some remnants of Lost Irem. It's also possible the Rite of Return wrecked the local Underworld for centuries, and Sin-Eaters are still dealing with the fallout.<br /> <br /> 3. Sin-Eaters stick to themselves and don't organize. Either it's because having a ghost in your head is not particularly emotionally healthy, or because there's a general stigma attached to the Bound (mortal or supernatural, or a bit of both). The Underworld doesn't really mesh right with mortal religions, Arisen cults won't take them, and Egypt at the time is crawling with necromantic problems. Many Sin-Eaters tend to be wanderer-in-the-wilderness types, stalking the dunes and alleyways as weird shamans.<br /> <br /> Any of these, or all three even, could exist in concurrence.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) I can see this option being especially prevalent in later eras, especially as the Cult of Osiris becomes more influential. In the period of the First Sothic Turn, I can see this being limited to the ranks of both the Silent Temple and the Cult of Anpu.<br /> <br /> 2) Very likely, especially the fact that they might occupy themselves with the fallout from Irem's collapse. I can even see such cults being nomadic by nature, especially since qhe Nameless Empire stretched far and wide.<br /> <br /> 3) Also likely, especially given how Sin-Eaters blur the lines between the living and the dead. Mortals would shy away from them, and the Hungry Dead could feel threatened in their presence.... and then there's the matter of the Su, who hunt them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=848356#post848356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Espritdecalamar, all of your options sound extremely appealing, but especially the second and third ones. I'll be sure to take them into account when we get around to Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> A little extra detail on the setting, including some highly speculative math on the supernatural population of First Turn Kemet.<br /> <br /> ... And now, a little fluff on how the Kindred of Kemet see the Strix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, great fluff on your end, Arcanist <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Will weave these to the main post (as docs) once I have time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T15:45:16-07:00","id":848447,"title":"","content":"Allow me a moment to say how pleased I am that this thread has passed the mikestone of having 1K views. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Moving on. Some random musings about how to depict the Cult of Wadjet in a Dark Eras setting. Recalling some ideas I had, I was thinking of tying them somehow to Shadow-related stuff, and considered two ways of doing this. <br /> <br /> One is to tie them somehow with the Hal and Afhal Usum, two choirs of snake spirits/Claimed from the Skinchangers supplement. <br /> <br /> Another would be to associate them somehow with the Razilu, the Snake Hosts. <br /> <br /> Neither option is mutually exclusive. Of course, I'm still working out the possible details on them. Plus, just to be sure, this is far enough from the Neolithic setting stuff that we can already assume the Gauntlet is up and running? Oh, wait, that probably is the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 03-16-2016, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T19:18:38-07:00","id":848553,"title":"","content":"The Neolithic setting was long before Irem and the Nameless Empire! So you're good on that front by a few thousand years at least.<br /> <br /> Also, hey, I'm curious. I was reading more of the Mumviri and it mentioned they're from the Land of Punt. That inspired me to look up more about the place, but there was very little to go on. Can you tell me a little about how you envisioned the place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T19:31:08-07:00","id":848559,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this is definitely post Gauntlet. My million dollar question is if it is also post-Oath of the Moon. I'm not even sure what I'm most excited for in Dark Eras any more. We may not have much that relates to the First Sothic Turn, but I'm hoping that the expansion of To the Strongest into Egypt (specifically with an eye on Mummy) will shed a bit more light into the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T19:49:34-07:00","id":848565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=848559#post848559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, this is definitely post Gauntlet. My million dollar question is if it is also post-Oath of the Moon. I'm not even sure what I'm most excited for in Dark Eras any more. We may not have much that relates to the First Sothic Turn, but I'm hoping that the expansion of To the Strongest into Egypt (specifically with an eye on Mummy) will shed a bit more light into the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>To the Strongest will also help me fleshing out more homebrew Dark Era stuff if I/we can continue this project beyond Age of Azar.<br /> <br /> As for whether it's post-Oath of the Moon, I'm leaning toward saying that it is. Especially since the Mimma Lemnua entry of the Shapechangers section made mention of the Wolf Gods.<br /> <br /> Also, I believe Arcanist suggested that the Pure may hold more influence in Kemet, while the Forsaken are the predominant half of the People in Mesopotamia (especially when you consider the material about them in the Chronicler's Guide).<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b><br /> I've also added in the GDoc where I'm putting my notes for Mummy House Rules. I would like to clarify as well that these were inspired, partially, by Pendragon's own 2E Conversion (as well as several other references here).<br /> <br /> A GDoc for the expanded Words of Irkalla Endowment by LostLight is also posted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 03-17-2016, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T22:56:22-07:00","id":848622,"title":"","content":"Neolithic Mage is about 2000 years before the Rite of Return is performed, FYI.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T23:01:43-07:00","id":848624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=848622#post848622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neolithic Mage is about 2000 years before the Rite of Return is performed, FYI.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that certainly is enough time for the Forsaken and Pure divisions to have formed with the Oath of the Moon's declaration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T07:24:36-07:00","id":848774,"title":"","content":"Some questions to ask of Bound of the Black Land:<br /> <br /> 1. What do they call themselves? &quot;Sin-Eater&quot; is a very instantiated term, so what would be culturally significant enough to be used to refer to the Bound? Ideally, I think it should be a term that both resonates with the culture of the time and place, but also a term that has fallen out of use and has been recycled by the Bound.<br /> <br /> 2. Sin-Eaters are always breaking laws. What metaphysical laws are they breaking in this age? What cultural mythoi are subverted by their very existence? I mentioned Osiris earlier; would comparisons invite sanctification or blasphemy?<br /> <br /> 3. What are geists? Beyond what the book says geists are, what are geists to Sin-Eaters here? When we think of ghosts nowadays we often think about emotional or psychic resonances. To the Kemetics, ghosts were an aspect of the soul, right? The Sheut or Ba or something detached from the rest after death? Is that how occultists view geists? How does that color impressions of the Bound? Do they have too much Ba? Or did they lose their Ba in the Bargain and have it replaced with the geist's own?<br /> <br /> 4. Are there any Bound Conspiracies afoot at the time? Does the Black Land have representatives of the Dzimba Woye? Or is it still too early for them? How about a Great Cult that goes all the way back to Irem (or at least claims such)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T07:50:50-07:00","id":849260,"title":"","content":"1. &quot;The Bound&quot; is quite possibly an appropriate term, but a word that had fallen out of use by the First Turn is 'Gala', a specialized Sumerian priesthood specifically meant to lament things, and were associated with Inanna and Ereshkigal.<br /> <br /> 2. The Gala were not easily defined in Sumerian society- they had no fixed gender identity, and were trained in a dialect of Sumerian used specifically to render the speech of goddesses called &quot;eme-sal&quot; the &quot;fine tongue&quot; or &quot;high-pitched voice&quot;. Despite that, many Gala were male and had large families. Their entire purpose was to lament, to appease the dead and ensure that the living continued to remember and sacrifice to them. Sumerian and Egyptian belief was that those without sacrifices suffered an uncomfortable life in the Underworld. In the CofD, this is literally true, as offerings and remembrance of the dead provides Essence. In Egypt, I'm not so sure they'd compare themselves to Osiris/Azar, but it is entirely possible they'd connect themselves with his dying and rising. This would make the Egyptian people rather upset, seeing as after being resurrected Osiris dutifully marched off to Duat to take up a throne there. The common response would likely be to cry &quot;Blasphemy!&quot; at least later. In the First Turn, the Osiris cult was just forming, and there was no real concept of homogenous or national religion. Association with Osiris would call upon his nature as God of Transition, aiding ghosts in moving on. Association with Anubis would call upon his nature as guide and protector of the dead. Osiris is the lord of the land of the dead, but it is Anubis who is god of the necropolis.<br /> <br /> 3. In Sumeria, they are the Gedim- simple as that. However, exactly <i>what </i>they are made of is a point of contention. Some Sumerian texts implied that the human soul was made up of three parts, and that two thirds of it moved on upon death, but the remaining third- which is either purely mortal or purely divine, it's hard to tell which -survives and becomes imprinted with the memories and emotions of the dead person, and are sustained by offerings. A Gedim risked becoming an Utukku by escaping the Underworld or being summoned by a priest, at which point their nature would be changed by the secondary transition and would become something else.<br /> <br /> To the Kemetic, they would be a strange kind of Akh. The Akh was the reunion of Ba and Ka that went on to the afterlife. The Ba was the personality of the person, while the Ka was their vitality- the Ka was lost during death, and restored by proper funerary rites and sustained by offerings. The Kemetic funerary priests had no way of knowing for sure whether the Se-Akh, a ritual to reunite Ba and Ka, worked properly, but it was implied that you could &quot;die a second time&quot; because of a botched ritual. Perhaps a Geist would be an Akh that either became powerful, or, is corrupt. It is no longer a sustained continuation of the person it was, but because of lax funerary practices or the destruction of its tomb, it was forced to wander. They might say that the Geist is an Akh without Ren- a dead person who has lost their name, and thus the core part of their identity. They tie themselves to the living to take advantage of their Ren, and possibly transition to the afterlife as a whole person, and in return the living person gets power- a second Ba and a second Ka, something that only gods are supposed to possess. This would be a disquieting situation to a devout follower of the Pesedjet, but some might feel pity for the corrupt Akh, even as they fight to keep a hold of their own Ren. Sin-Eater Manifestations are the manipulation of different parts of their soul. There are eleven Manifestations, and I think most of these map to the parts of the soul in Egyptian belief.<br /> <br /> 4. Don't quite remember the Dzimba Woye, but there is no way there <i>isn't </i>a Conspiracy. The Ancient Egyptians were thorough in their attempts to separate the living and the dead, although paradoxically, they didn't have a concept of death as such, only a distinct and final transition that is not deviated against. Such a deviation is against Ma'at. The Sumerians, the Canaanites, etc. all believed in death as a final transition, and they didn't believe in a potential paradise like the Egyptians did, but they also didn't separate the ancestors from the living the way the people of Kemet did. Heck, they didn't even really think of a ghost as <i>being </i>the same person, but a different creature with the person's memories. Doesn't appear that they made an important distinction between the two, however, and the ancestors were still a part of regular life. The Kemetic, however, banished the dead to the west bank of the Nile and there was minimal contact with the ancestors beyond specifically going to the tomb and making offerings there. The living go on to their own lives, and leave the dead in their necropoli.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T08:03:11-07:00","id":849269,"title":"","content":"That is some fascinating stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T08:17:34-07:00","id":849276,"title":"","content":"I second that sentiment, espiritdecalmar.<br /> <br /> Looking at this, Gala could be a term for Sin-Eaters, while Gedim is for Geister. And I also agree that Bound is still a good term for that time period.<br /> <br /> Also, could anyone look around to see if <i>Setem</i> is an actual Egyptian term. I remember reading it somewhere that said it was a term for priests of Anubis. If so, maybe it could also be a term that some Sin-Eaters may identify themselves with?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T08:26:30-07:00","id":849726,"title":"","content":"It is Setem, yes, but they were less priests of Anpu and more generic funerary priests who wore Anpu masks while embalming the dead. In Hieratic, it would be spelled Stm, because the language doesn't naturally have written vowels.<br /> <br /> And now, the different Sin-Eater Manifestations and how they relate to the Kemetic anatomy of the soul. Several of these are the more immediately recognizable parts of the soul anatomy, especially since they're the Pillars of the Arisen soul- Ab, Ba, Ka, Ren, Sheut. The others are less well-recognized. The Khat is your natural body, while the Sahu is your spiritual replacement of it. The Khu is distantly related to the Akh, being the immortal part of a person that helped catalyze the Se-Akh and put the Ba and Ka back together in the Sahu. Alternatively, the Khu actually <i>was </i>the Akh, and it was a separate part of the soul that lived in the Sahu and needed the Ba and Ka to properly animate it. Whatever the case, the Khu was the immortal, imperishable, 'Divine Spark'-like part of you. Sekhem is sometimes also said to be a part of the soul, the radiant life force of the body while the Ka was the animating force of the spirit that could separate out into a different entity and could be the source of ghosts.<br /> <br /> The anatomy of the soul is, understandably, complex and contradictory in Kemetic writing, and doubly so with modern Egyptologists who just have the texts to go on.<br /> <br /> <b>Boneyard: </b>Ba<br /> <b>Caul: </b>Khat<br /> <b>Curse: </b>Ren<br /> <b>Marionette: </b>Ka<br /> <b>Oracle: </b>Khu<br /> <b>Pit: </b>Sheut<br /> <b>Rage:</b> Ab<br /> <b>Shroud: </b>Sahu<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T18:55:35-07:00","id":849959,"title":"","content":"I have now set up a GDoc for the Akhu and Khat Archetypes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T19:16:31-07:00","id":849965,"title":"","content":"So, I have a question that may require brass iron balls to ask, but I'm asking anyhow: has anyone given consideration to creating a fan-made adventure?<br /> <br /> Back in the day on the Planescape fan site, we put together an entire module to introduce people to the game. It would be really cool to do something like that for Age of Azar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 03-19-2016, 10:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T19:36:37-07:00","id":849976,"title":"","content":"We have not, as of yet, but that does sound like an incredible idea. One overly ambitious project at a time though. We're still thinking through Geist and Mummy conversions, though we're well on our way with both. Following that, I'm also working on a blue book fan supplement on the side for handling Cults.<br /> <br /> That being said, this is an open invite thread. Anyone who wants to contribute any ideas or material is totally open to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T20:05:28-07:00","id":849982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=849965#post849965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I have a question that may require brass iron balls to ask, but I'm asking anyhow: has anyone given consideration to creating a fan-made adventure?<br /> <br /> Back in the day on the Planescape fan site, we put together an entire module to introduce people to the game. It would be really cool to do something like that for Age of Azar.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Arcanist pointed out, this is an open invite. Anyone is welcome to contributing ideas here.<br /> <br /> Regarding a fan-made adventure, it would be interesting to have one which deals with Apep's eventual release and rampage. I'm sure that can inspire a lot of ideas, yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T20:20:40-07:00","id":849989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=849982#post849982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As Arcanist pointed out, this is an open invite. Anyone is welcome to contributing ideas here.<br /> <br /> Regarding a fan-made adventure, it would be interesting to have one which deals with Apep's eventual release and rampage. I'm sure that can inspire a lot of ideas, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you'd have an entire adventure path on your hands with that hook! It sound like a cool idea, I'll do some digging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T20:28:44-07:00","id":849994,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that our intention was that when Apep is released he ends up aiding the Shunankhsen and their army of Amkhata in their battle against the Arisen. This would likely be the climactic scene of the Story, with Utterances flying everywhere and Manifested Spirit Spawn of Apep falling upon the Arisen and Sadikh. It will be a battle of serious magical madness.<br /> <br /> I've got some ideas brewing myself, now, but first things first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T21:27:25-07:00","id":850021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=849994#post849994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind that our intention was that when Apep is released he ends up aiding the Shunankhsen and their army of Amkhata in their battle against the Arisen. This would likely be the climactic scene of the Story, with Utterances flying everywhere and Manifested Spirit Spawn of Apep falling upon the Arisen and Sadikh. It will be a battle of serious magical madness.<br /> <br /> I've got some ideas brewing myself, now, but first things first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no doubt! Hence why I said &quot;whole adventure path.&quot; I've got so ideas too. I'd really like to see Geist since it gets so little love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T21:30:42-07:00","id":850025,"title":"","content":"We're actually jumping straight into Geist right now. Not necessarily from just a First Turn perspective, but as a 2e hack in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T08:51:19-07:00","id":850589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=848553#post848553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, hey, I'm curious. I was reading more of the Mumviri and it mentioned they're from the Land of Punt. That inspired me to look up more about the place, but there was very little to go on. Can you tell me a little about how you envisioned the place?</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, Punt wasn't an easy one- not only there is little to no information about it, it looks like CofD took a different path from the general consensus about its location (from what I could gather, most researchers locate it in the Horn of Africa, but CofD seem to placed it in South Africa and connect it to Mutapa, as it was hinted by Dave). Using that connection, I've made some research and decided to base its concept loosely around the Shona people and their culture. When writing the Mumvuri, I've thought about a sophisticated culture based around harsh divisions of totems and tribes, connection to the spirit world and some sort of &quot;high shamanism&quot;, including lineages of all kinds of shapeshifters which are contained to certain tribes and a &quot;Parliament of Beasts&quot; where the leaders of all local Breeds meet together in the shadows of the world. In that culture of spirit animals and werebeasts, the Mumvuri are an anomaly- they belong to a totem which should not exist, yet that totem is enough to give them proper presentation. It is a wild land, a sophisticated land, a place of dark mysteries and shiny treasures for those who dare to pass the guardian beasts and undead witches of Punt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 03-21-2016, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T16:50:27-07:00","id":851447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=850589#post850589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah, Punt wasn't an easy one- not only there is little to no information about it, it looks like CofD took a different path from the general consensus about its location (from what I could gather, most researchers locate it in the Horn of Africa, but CofD seem to placed it in South Africa and connect it to Mutapa, as it was hinted by Dave). Using that connection, I've made some research and decided to base its concept loosely around the Shona people and their culture. When writing the Mumvuri, I've thought about a sophisticated culture based around harsh divisions of totems and tribes, connection to the spirit world and some sort of &amp;quot;high shamanism&amp;quot;, including lineages of all kinds of shapeshifters which are contained to certain tribes and a &amp;quot;Parliament of Beasts&amp;quot; where the leaders of all local Breeds meet together in the shadows of the world. In that culture of spirit animals and werebeasts, the Mumvuri are an anomaly- they belong to a totem which should not exist, yet that totem is enough to give them proper presentation. It is a wild land, a sophisticated land, a place of dark mysteries and shiny treasures for those who dare to pass the guardian beasts and undead witches of Punt.</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually makes me think of what little I read on the Hengeyokai from WoD. Which isn't entirely a bad thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T19:42:35-07:00","id":851534,"title":"","content":"I just got Dreams of Avarice, so expect a ton of Mummy fluff incoming soon. Also, ideas for Kemetic Werewolves and Changing Breeds are brewing and coming close to fruition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T20:38:24-07:00","id":851554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=851534#post851534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just got Dreams of Avarice, so expect a ton of Mummy fluff incoming soon. Also, ideas for Kemetic Werewolves and Changing Breeds are brewing and coming close to fruition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I happen to have an incomplete fluff document on Kemet's Uratha. Will send it to you by PM in a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T13:20:09-07:00","id":854184,"title":"","content":"So, one of the easiest &quot;ins&quot; for the Uratha in Kemet is the Upper Egyptian god known as Wepwawet, the wolf-headed god of war and death, sometimes considered a child of Anpu, other times considered their equal. Wepwawet had two cities which had massive cult centres dedicated to them, Zawty (later called Lycopolis and know Asyut) and Abdju. You might recognize the latter as Abydos, the Arisen necropolis they ruled openly as god-kings in the First Turn.<br /> <br /> Our current musings are leaning towards Bone Shadows being the most common Tribe in Kemet at the time, based in Zawty, with a Ghost Wolf Lodge in Abdju that may, or may not, be dedicated to Anpu himself. Regardless, the Abdju Uratha are likely as swept up in the affairs of the Arisen as anyone else, considering Wolf-Blooded aren't immune to the throes of Sybaris. Picture a Su-Menet Guildmaster with a pack of Uratha at their back. That's something horrific to behold, and certainly gives an excellent explanation as to how the Arisen were able to handle Apep with a Lodge of Ghost Wolves on their side of the great battle at the end of Unas' reign.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the Changing Breeds aren't absent in Kemet, and in fact likely outnumber the Uratha. The Bastet form a privileged few in the arms of the cult at Per-Bast, the Baal-Hadad are doing well under the auspices of the Apis cult, and the Distant Ones reside in the city of Nekhen, quite possibly support the cult of Nekhbet in their sister-city across the Nile.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> Additional material on Arisen/Kemetic views of Ghosts, Geists, and Sin-Eaters coming soon after further scrutiny of The Litany of the Fivefold Soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T14:04:16-07:00","id":854199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=854184#post854184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, one of the easiest &quot;ins&quot; for the Uratha in Kemet is the Upper Egyptian god known as Wepwawet, the wolf-headed god of war and death, sometimes considered a child of Anpu, other times considered their equal. Wepwawet had two cities which had massive cult centres dedicated to them, Zawty (later called Lycopolis and know Asyut) and Abdju. You might recognize the latter as Abydos, the Arisen necropolis they ruled openly as god-kings in the First Turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAs a heads-up, Upuaut/Wepwawet has some coverage in The Pack.<br /> <br /> \u200bEdit: It's just a little bit of coverage. But if you want to know it sooner rather than later, ask Stew to reveal the Lodge of Garm write-up on the blog post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","user":"Acrozatarim","date":". 03-27-2016, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://foru