e choose between the nascent tribe of undead hunting and the lodge that worships an Egyptian god? You're too cruel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T15:40:23-07:00","id":854234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=854202#post854202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, this is going to get <i>very</i> interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Veryyyyyy interesting indeed. I wonder what Stew takes his bribes and ritual sacrifices in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T21:32:14-07:00","id":854356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=854199#post854199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a heads-up, Upuaut/Wepwawet has some coverage in The Pack.<br /> <br /> \u200bEdit: It's just a little bit of coverage. But if you want to know it sooner rather than later, ask Stew to reveal the Lodge of Garm write-up on the blog post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>Damn. I guess I was kinda expecting a reply from you or any of the other big names here in this thread. But you definitely caught me by surprise with this bombshell. Thank you, good sir.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=854202#post854202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, this is going to get <i>very</i> interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, it is. And on a semi-related note, the 1.5k+ views here already has me hoping for this open project to become a sticky.<br /> :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 03-28-2016, 06:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T08:57:34-07:00","id":854502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=854226#post854226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you gonna make me choose between the nascent tribe of undead hunting and the lodge that worships an Egyptian god? You're too cruel.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I <i>think </i>he's suggesting that the Lodge of Garm will have details on the Lodge that worships said Egyptian god. Maybe. Not entirely sure.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> Alright, so, the Litany of the Fivefold Soul. Fascinating stuff, it's basically an abbreviated version of the Iremite &quot;Book of Going Forth By Day&quot; (IE. The Book of the Dead), but it seems that unlike the later Kemetic versions, the Iremites had no fallbacks for if you screwed up. You screwed up, and your soul fell to pieces and was eaten by Ammut, the Slaughterers, and other horrible things that live in Duat. In the Book of Going Forth By Day, there are spells written that act as failsafes in the case of the omission, failure, and/or inability to continue certain funerary conditions. No relatives able to feed the Ka with offerings? No problem, there's a spell for that. The heart is destroyed? No problem- scarab amulet for that. Spells to remember your Name, spells to preserve the Ba, spells to uphold the Shadow- failsafes like you wouldn't believe. The Kemetic people were <i>very </i>serious about the afterlife.<br /> <br /> The Iremites, even more so. No failsafes in case you forget things, but the would-be Deathless went down to Duat with Utterances inscribed on their Sekhem to aid their passage and ensure their survival. Not <i>quite </i>the same as a pile of failsafes, nor as reassuring, but the Iremites weren't exactly a touchy-feely caring culture. Most importantly, it seems as though there are some <i>distinct </i>differences between the later Kemetic interpretations of the Soul Anatomy and the Iremite interpretation (at least according to the Litany).<br /> <br /> <b>Ab: </b>In the Iremite tradition, this is probably what we would traditionally call &quot;the soul&quot;. It is the repository of Memory, of emotion, of passion, of will, and the record of all the things that you have done with your life. To 'stray from Deathlessness' was to try and go against the flow of Nebthet and attempt to return to the land of the living, which would shatter the five-fold soul and send the Heart down to Duat alone, where none of the other Pillars could support or protect it, and it would be a sitting duck for Ammut's maw. The Heart is more than just your ability to feel, it is your ability to <i>control </i>those feelings, for passing the Second Gate of Duat requires you to resist the passions that assault your Heart- lost loves, old enemies, etc. It is worth noting that in the Kemetic tradition, the Heart is weighed against Ma'at, and if it is heavier (IE. full of sin) then it is given to the Devourer. Given Dreams of Avarice, to have a heavy Heart is to have one weighed down with suffering and punishment. You will have been broken and bound by the Law of Suffering, and thus have become a fitting sacrifice for Ammut.<br /> <br /> <b>Ba: </b>In the Kemetic tradition, the personality, the mental/spiritual self that leaves and returns to the body and takes the form of a human-headed bird. In the Iremite tradition, it is the Spirit, and appears to take on aspects of the Ka from the Kemetic tradition, being a sort of &quot;spirit double&quot; of the Ab. The Litany says that should the five-fold soul shatter, the Ba will return and possess your corpse, which will then be burnt as an abomination, which could mean that it's the source of ghosts in Iremite belief. (References to rising, being a Lifeless abomination, and burning, plus the bird aesthetic, makes it hard to not think Strix, admittedly.) Whatever the case, the Ba is driven, it is impulsive, and it is definitely impressive. The Ba refuses to quit when other things do, and it will endure stubbornly beyond death, even when everything in the living world is screaming at it that it shouldn't exist. It's my personal opinion that this is <i>definitely </i>the part of the five-fold soul that ghosts come from.<br /> <br /> <b>Ka: </b>The Essence, the vital spark that empowers the Ba in Kemetic belief, and apparently so in Iremite belief as well. It can be sustained with offerings, spells, and acts of remembrance. The Ka is empowering, the thing that gives energy to life, but is different than Sekhem, which is the luminous, radiant lifeforce upon which the entire soul is built. The parts of the soul might be of different qualities, but Sekhem is the thing they're all made of. It appears as though Essence is <i>literally </i>Essence in the CofD sense, as the Litany describes the shattered soul's Ka mingling in &quot;oases and sacred places&quot; and that &quot;witches and unnatural things&quot; will make use of it. Loci, anyone? What interests me about this passage, is that there is a distinct difference between sorcerers, which appear to be acceptable from an Iremite point of view, and witches, which are unacceptable, serve their enemies, and make unholy use of part of the soul. It also explicitly calls out other Essence-using creatures as 'unnatural', which is interesting seeing as Spirits are literally animistic reflections of the world, and Pangaeans have been called &quot;pillars&quot; of the world, with more on that to be elaborated in The Sundered World in the Dark Era Companion. I know that the Vinca Mages make use of the stone hearts of Pangaean gods as menhirs, but now I'm wondering if some made their way into pillars, idols, and altars in Irem.<br /> <br /> <b>Ren: </b>The Name, which in Kemetic belief existed as the repository of your identity. It is no different in the CofD, as true names are a thing that the Deathless, amongst others, make a big deal out of. The Heart might contain the literal memories, sensations, and human experiences of life, but it appears to be the Name that translates that into <i>identity</i>. The Name protected everything else, partially by ensuring that the deceased would be remembered and the appropriate rituals to protect the other Pillars would be performed, but also acting as a <i>definition</i> for the rest. The Name translates Ab, Ba, Ka, and Sheut from ineffable intangibles into a person- something knowable, something memorable, something comprehensible. The Name is the anchor to which everything else is affixed. The Litany describes a Decree as a declaration of identity, but the footnotes complicate it. Decree means more than that simple word, it also means &quot;I become&quot; or &quot;I choose to be&quot; or, perhaps most importantly, &quot;I am&quot;. It is worth noting that the hymns of the Deceived Temakh are long litanies of descriptors, of facets of their identity, and that end, always, in &quot;I am&quot;. I have come to the conclusion that those poems are, in some way, their true names rendered in such a way as mortals can attempt to understand. The fate of the Name of a shattered soul is to be forgotten, and being a forgotten ghost means losing Essence, and losing Anchors, until you are consigned to the Great Below.<br /> <br /> <b>Sheut: </b>The Shadow, a dark reflection of a person that contains something of who they are, it appears as though the Shadow is the repository of secrets, of truths, and of death itself. I honestly have very little to say about the Sheut as a literal piece of the soul anatomy, and more about it as a metaphor (which could be the same thing? Idk). Most Affinities and Utterances based around Sheut are based around, either the dead, Morality/Integrity, or secrets, revelations, and mysteries. The Sheut is more than a Shadow, it is the Darkness, and this revelation really made it click for me. The Shadow is the inherent nature of the CofD as expounded into a specific person. It is death, it is secrets, and it is mysteries. But more importantly than all that, the Sheut is the inherent monstrosity of a person, that great alluring darkness deep within, and it is mastery of the Sheut that allows you to overcome that and grow beyond it. Avoiding mastery/knowledge of the Shadow is to put a pretty mask over a monster, and pretending to be more than an animal while still struggling with your baser nature. Also worth noting is that the Litany describes the Sheut as &quot;howling&quot; in Twilight so that mortals will curse it. Another potential source of ghosts, or possibly something worse?<br /> <br /> The Sahu, being your spirit-flesh, appears to be mingled self-image and inherent truth/identity. The Akhu is someone who survives with their soul intact and gains power in the afterlife. By that definition, all Deathless are Akhu and need only rebuild their Pillars, but they are Akhu in service to the Judges. A Deathless in Apotheosis is a <i>true </i>Akhu, a free person with magical power, the Pillars of their soul united, able to ascend to A'aru. A Sin-Eater would be someone who specializes in aiding ghosts, either the Ba or Sheut of the dead, in putting themselves back together so that they may go to the afterlife whole and pass the Weighing of the Heart. Vampires are, honestly, a lot worse off than I earlier thought. They've been stripped of Ba and Ka, and must devour it from others. Their Sheut threatens to overtake them, and their Ren is slowly crumbling. As for the Ab? I honestly don't know. You could probably say that a Vampire is someone who has &quot;eaten their heart&quot; (IE. To escape justice), in which case they are Lifeless monstrosities desperately trying to shore up their Ren to make up for a lack of everything else and resist an unfettered and untempered Sheut, stealing Ka from the living. It could be that post-mortem Embrace leaves certain Mekhet Hollow because it rips their soul from the path to Duat, leaving their Ba behind, while a normal Embrace binds the Ba to the body. The Strix, though, are <i>definitely </i>unions of Ba and Sheut or, heck, even just Sheut. Or Ba. Depends on your perspective. I'm leaning towards Ba &amp; Sheut or just Sheut myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T12:44:09-07:00","id":854608,"title":"","content":"Now <i>these</i> are some interesting notes you got here, Arcanist. Especially those with regards to other supernaturals. And I can definitely picture better an antagonistic relationship towards Mages and Werewolves during the days of Irem.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Werewolves, I assume Ka or Ba would be their defining Pillar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T13:48:37-07:00","id":854643,"title":"","content":"I can see vampires as lacking an Ab, and being overwhelmed by an out of balance Ba. Mages are those consumed by their Ren and Sheut, blinded by secrets and truths. <br /> <br /> Here's a fun one; what do the Pillars of a Promethean look like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T14:46:39-07:00","id":854682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=854643#post854643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a fun one; what do the Pillars of a Promethean look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Patchwork, and on Fire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T15:28:24-07:00","id":854696,"title":"","content":"I'd probably say that Prometheans don't even <i>have </i>Pillars because they don't have a soul. Sekhem, and thus Pillars, seems to be a function of the human soul, and static life in general. Sekhem is predictable, it can be shaped, it follows cycles, and even though it shares some superficial characteristics with Pyros, the two are very, very different forces. Sekhem is what <b>is</b> while Pyros is what <b>may be</b>. So I'd probably say that a Promethean wouldn't appear to have Sekhem or Pillars to one of the Arisen, which would probably distress them greatly.<br /> <br /> On a goofier, more cosmological note, if Sekhem is likened to Nuclear Waste in the chapter To The Strongest, then perhaps Azoth is like active nuclear fission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T16:29:01-07:00","id":862259,"title":"","content":"For your reading pleasure: The Sekhmeti, a homebrew Bloodline<br /> <br /> The ancient Egyptians tell a story of the mythical past, where men conspired against the will of the gods; Ra, god of the sun, sent forth one of his Eyes in the shape of Sekhmet, a furious lioness, in order to slay the wicked. Yet Sekhmet's bloodlust was not sated by the slaughter of the men she had been sent to kill, and set about the murder of the entire human race. The only way to end her rampage was a trick by the gods in which Sekhmet was given copious amounts of alcohol (dyed red, so as to pass as blood) that eventually incapacitated her; drunk and calmed, she transformed into the domestic cat Bast, and was appeased by yearly rituals so that she might never again threaten to consume humanity.<br /> <br /> This story paints a far kinder picture of events than what truly transpired. Sekhmet did not peacefully fall, nor was she quickly tamed and forgiven; the gods lashed her with the fire of the sun and drove her into the unyielding desert, banishing the red-stained horror to suffer eternally in the lonesome night. Hiding beneath the sands during the day and sneaking forth under the stars to kill again, the lioness cultivated a brood of lesser servants to act as extensions of her will. As a fallen god, she imbued them with immense power; as a patron of warriors, she trained them in the ways of battle. Full after a grand slaughter that consumed an entire Egyptian city, Sekhmet retreated into the red lands of the desert and trusted her creations to handle themselves, never to be seen again.<br /> <br /> The Sekhmeti name themselves after their supposed patron goddess, but the long ages since Egypt's pagan heyday have diluted their identity to simply being Lions. They are few in number, and most are immeasurably ancient, dating back to well before the rise of monotheism; they rarely Embrace from the modern humans who have forgotten the true faith from so long ago. The Sekhmeti preach a creed with few tenets - love for their distant feline mother, utter hatred for the sun and the masculine god who condemned them, and disdain for civilization stemming from being cast out of it so long ago - and largely steer clear of wider vampire society. <br /> <br /> Some conspire to find and reawaken the fury of their lost progenitor, while others are content to merely survive the march of history and quietly plot the end of the sunlit world. A handful of the Sekhmeti rise to prominence in the Circle of the Crone, and others would likely enjoy the more revolutionary and anarchic factions of the Carthian Movement, but the vast majority of the bloodline are apolitical recluses.<br /> <br /> Nickname: Lions<br /> <br /> Parent Clan: Gangrel <br /> <br /> Bloodline Disciplines: Animalism, Protean, Resilience, Vigor <br /> <br /> Bloodline Bane: The Sekhmeti count their Humanity as two lower than its actual rating for the sake of determining damage from sunlight. In addition, the eyes of the Sekhmeti flash like those of one possessed by the Strix, causing many in the wider Kindred community to scorn them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 04-16-2016, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T18:14:23-07:00","id":862323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <