> </div>Perhaps the Sandharrowed kith Blessing might be a good place to start?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T17:35:16-07:00","id":863398,"title":"","content":"Posting these little tidbits from the To the Strongest Chapter for Dark Eras, since they'll help work out the Awakened segment of Age of Azar. <hr /><br /> Path - Pillar<br /> ==========<br /> Acanthus - Ren<br /> Mastigos - Ba<br /> Moros - Sheut<br /> Obrimos - Ka<br /> Thyrsus - Ab<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> Also, in contrast to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=854502#post854502\">Iremite disdain for 'witches'</a> mentioned by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a>, I think I can safely say that the Hemka of the Weret-Hekau may have been among the more respected supernaturals of the Black Land. Heck, they might have even grown out of the traditions set down by Imhotep when you consider the following statement, paraphrased from the Dark Eras book.<br /> <br /> &quot;\u200bThe first Weret-Hekau texts date back to the dawn of the Old Kingdom, and describe an even earlier age. The Predynastic peoples prospered under the direct rule of the gods, who taught them agriculture, crafts and the power of Sekhem, the subtle energy of all existence. These god-rulers built the foundations of Kemet\u2019s culture by reshaping Sekhem, but the project slipped out of their control, and disaster struck. In response, he ancestors of the Weret-Hekau founded the tradition of erasing dangerous knowledge, to ensure that few signs of the earlier \u201cScorpion Dynasty\u201d remain. But these early magi studied before they destroyed.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T14:16:38-07:00","id":866112,"title":"","content":"Loving the drawn up Sekhmeti. It's been a while since I've read Vampire, but isn't a function of Protean turning into a mist-form? Perhaps the Sekhmeti, or the Habiru in general, chose to turn into blowing sand instead. A swirling sandstorm racing towards you, flaying your skin and drinking your blood. Red Land indeed.<br /> <br /> As a side note, exams are almost done for me and I'll have a lot more time to dedicate to my homebrew projects. This includes my Cult work, which I fully intend to port over to here, and other stuff based around First Turn Kemet. I fully intend to elaborate on this setting to the best of my ability, and I've got some spectacular ideas waiting in the wings.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Considering opening up another thread to discuss a collaborative Neolithic setting. The stuff I've seen in spoilers from The Sundered World is getting the creative juices flowing. I'm also getting ideas on how to make a setting during the reign of the Nameless Empire, including how to represent the mortal members of the Guilds. It will be a little hollow until the Dark Eras Companion comes out, and I eagerly await seeing the rules for Sekhem Sorcerers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 04-15-2016, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T11:12:53-07:00","id":866459,"title":"","content":"I have added a (still incomplete) intro doc for Mages in Age of Azar up on the main post.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"