category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=875309#post875309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even so, that shouldn't stop us from trying to imagine how Egyptian Hemka perceive the Aeons of the other Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh certainly. Though part of me likes the idea of drawing on some contemporary neighboring cultures for some of them... let me do some quick review, I'll be back in a sec.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T00:16:11-07:00","id":875389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=875309#post875309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even so, that shouldn't stop us from trying to imagine how Egyptian Hemka perceive the Aeons of the other Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm thinking, preceding their future Abrahamic personas, the Aeons of Forces and Prime have Canaanite personas - specifically those of Baal Hadad, and Atharte (the Caananite version of Ishtar). The Weret-Hekau equate these figures with Horus and Hathor/Sekhmet* respectively.<br /> <br /> *Ishtar is both a war goddess and a sex/fertility goddess. Hathor/Sekhmet have the same duality, but its more extreme in that she has different identities for the two roles.<br /> <br /> Their imagery is also influenced by the solar snake-wielding mother goddess, and lunar earth-shacking bull-god of the Minoans (I can't pull names here, because we have no idea what they were named).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-27-2016, 03:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T01:16:04-07:00","id":875421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=875389#post875389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking, preceding their future Abrahamic personas, the Aeons of Forces and Prime have Canaanite personas - specifically those of Baal Hadad, and Atharte (the Caananite version of Ishtar). The Weret-Hekau equate these figures with Horus and Hathor/Sekhmet* respectively.<br /> <br /> *Ishtar is both a war goddess and a sex/fertility goddess. Hathor/Sekhmet have the same duality, but its more extreme in that she has different identities for the two roles.<br /> <br /> Their imagery is also influenced by the solar snake-wielding mother goddess, and lunar earth-shacking bull-god of the Minoans (I can't pull names here, because we have no idea what they were named).</div> </div> </div> </div>That definitely works. Hmm. And what about the Aeons of the other Arcana? Got anything yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T01:22:06-07:00","id":875425,"title":"","content":"Tinkering... the Aeon of Matter is yet to &quot;congeal&quot; into the distinct form of the monstrous mother Ekidna - she is still the vast sea from which all matter arises. She is called Naunet or Nammu (Sumerian).<br /> <br /> The terrifying Aeon of Death swims in her waters. Some call him Apep, but whether he or the Idigam had the name first, none can say.<br /> <br /> The Mages of Mesopotamia will remember them as Tiamat and Qingu even after they evolve into their imprisoned Greek personas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-27-2016, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T02:28:49-07:00","id":875443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=875425#post875425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tinkering... the Aeon of Matter is yet to &amp;quot;congeal&amp;quot; into the distinct form of the monstrous mother Ekidna - she is still the vast sea from which all matter arises. She is called Naunet or Nammu (Sumerian).<br /> <br /> The terrifying Aeon of Death swims in her waters. Some call him Apep, but whether he or the Idigam had the name first, none can say.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about Spirit and Life? I assume the Snake is still the former, and perhaps the latter could be a Bird instead of a Stag?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T06:16:13-07:00","id":875548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=875443#post875443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How about Spirit and Life? I assume the Snake is still the former, and perhaps the latter could be a Bird instead of a Stag?</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;To the Strongest&quot; write up implies to me that they hadn't settled on fixed animal personas, yet - so allowing them BOTH some culture by culture variance in this era as well, how about Hippopotamus/Crocodile for Life (Taweret) and Ibis/Baboon for Spirit (Djehutey) in the tradition of Khemetic Mages?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T06:49:24-07:00","id":875573,"title":"","content":"Hello again- waking up from a bit of hibernation for some more fluff.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Awakened Perceptions on Seba</b></u><br /> <br /> The Awakened of Kemet know the work of the Nameless Empire well, the Relics they left behind also concealing secrets of their sorcery, and providing numerous Mysterties for the Hemka. By the union of <i>heka</i>- free, almost gaseous Sekhem that can be shaped through architecture and guided by Will -and their Ba, they build a silver ladder to A'aru, where they marked their True Name upon the Scroll of Ages and attained the mysteries of the gods for themselves. No sorcerer-kings would conceal this lore from them now, no Guilds restrict the flow of this knowledge to the common folk. But the Hemka must be wary to abide by Ma'at, or else they provoke Apep, the serpent, by breaking the limbs of Nut with their arts.<br /> <br /> In death, the Awakened, too, descend to Duat for judgement, and hopefully ascend to starry A'aru. Their Pillars persist after death, but what becomes of their Sekhem? The Sekhem that empowered the Hemka when they were alive was shaped into Attainments to better channel the flow of <i>heka</i>, the Awakened seized hold of <i>dedwen</i> and true names and filled them to bursting with the sweet incense of <i>heka</i>, working sorcery from afar. With great trepidation and proper respect, they used <i>heka </i>as a smith's tongs to handle pure manifest Sekhem. In death, the Sekhem upon which their Pillars rested persists, and it returns into the world as wondrous relics and gleaming stars- the Seba.<br /> <br /> This is not the only source for these glorious and terrible Relics, for mad artisans may still seize hold of the <i>heka </i>in their work and shape it, but the mightiest of Seba stem either from the long-lost arts of the Scorpion Dynasty, or the souls of the Hemka. Many powerful willworkers of Kemet will often cast spells to be sure of the time, place, and means of their death so that those important to them may receive the mystical bounty shaped by their deeds and how they have marked the Scroll. However, despite these beliefs, it is extremely difficult to tell if a Seba forms in the wake of the death of one of the Awakened, or is simply an unbound Seba attracted to a powerful working of Word and Will for a period of convergence.<br /> <br /> The Left-Handed of the Black Land are those unscrupulous sorcerers who steal Seba, depriving the Awakened community of the final masterpiece of a life dedicated to magical works and the following of Ma'at. These same Left-Handed are also those who would defy the need to descend to Duat, eating their hearts and binding their soul to their Sheut, persisting as a restless shade, consuming the Ka of others in order to continue their wretched existence. Some, even more horrific, devour souls in a mad attempt to harvest the Sekhem within, and these horrific sorcerers are often servants of the Devourer, and those who purposely provoke Apep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T07:07:51-07:00","id":875593,"title":"","content":"On the Mind and Space Aeon(s), I'm thinking they don't have their shared vessel yet. Instead they have no vessel. They are both bodiless intelligences even in the context of the Astral. The Weret-Hekau knows them as Amun (Space) and Amunet (Mind). Their palace is an open air temple of countless pillars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T12:40:24-07:00","id":875865,"title":"","content":"Just noticed that Hunting Grounds: Sumer is actually set a few centuries AFTER the First Turn. I was already consideringa revision of that setting for 2nd Edition, including (given how relatively recent it turns out the Sundering was) the idea that it's pre-Oaths of the Moon. The Uratha are trying to claim a new role for themselves, and the failure of the era leads to the Oaths to Luna and the Firstborn and birth of the Tribes.<br /> <br /> What do you think of the Oaths of the Moon still being in the future during the First Turn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T14:23:25-07:00","id":875981,"title":"","content":"I love Sumerian werewolves, and it's one of the most awesome things from Werewolf: the Forsaken. Pre-Oaths of the Moon makes sense for how different the werewolves are, and the lack of Tribes. However, the Pure on the outskirts will have to be changed to something else, basically a kind of proto-Pure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T15:21:33-07:00","id":876048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=875981#post875981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love Sumerian werewolves, and it's one of the most awesome things from Werewolf: the Forsaken. Pre-Oaths of the Moon makes sense for how different the werewolves are, and the lack of Tribes. However, the Pure on the outskirts will have to be changed to something else, basically a kind of proto-Pure.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wouldn't they all be kinda &quot;Pure&quot;? Isn't this before the Forsaken returned to Luna for forgiveness? Or does that predate the Oath of the Moon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T15:22:45-07:00","id":876049,"title":"","content":"If you ever do write out Hunting Ground: Sumer for 2E, it'd be nice to add it here in a &quot;What is to Come&quot; section of Age of Azar.<br /> <br /> That said, I also remember someone considered making a chronicle that concerns Apep the Idigam. And i'll see if I can get around to putting up an abridged overview of the setting and its history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T15:26:38-07:00","id":876052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=876048#post876048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wouldn't they all be kinda &quot;Pure&quot;? Isn't this before the Forsaken returned to Luna for forgiveness? Or does that predate the Oath of the Moon?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From Sundered World what makes the Pure 'Pure' is just ripping out their Auspice, so anyone one that had their Auspice would still react liek a Forsaken rules wise","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T15:59:56-07:00","id":876073,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... The idea that between Sundering and Oath all Werewolves were Auspiceless because Luna had turned on them would make a certain amount of sense. It'd be a change from 1E Hunting Grounds Ancient Sumer, but I'm fine with that as we adjust the material to new canon.<br /> <br /> It'd make it the case that the Pure are those clinging to their pre-Oath state, seeing Luna's returned blessing as the &quot;corruption&quot; they are Pure of.<br /> <br /> My thinking on the fully controlled indefinite Garu form, and the reduced Lunacy, is that it's a feat facilitated by proximity to the fetish-brick Ziggurat - a working of magic against the nature of the Uratha that would be considered blasphemous by the post-Oath Forsaken.<br /> <br /> So it wouldn't apply in the wilderness beyond Bau or any similar settlements.<br /> <br /> I wonder what Bau's relations with Kish are like...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T16:18:43-07:00","id":876096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=876073#post876073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... The idea that between Sundering and Oath all Werewolves were Auspiceless because Luna had turned on them would make a certain amount of sense. It'd be a change from 1E Hunting Grounds Ancient Sumer, but I'm fine with that as we adjust the material to new canon.<br /> <br /> It'd make it the case that the Pure are those clinging to their pre-Oath state, seeing Luna's returned blessing as the &amp;quot;corruption&amp;quot; they are Pure of.<br /> <br /> My thinking on the fully controlled indefinite Garu form, and the reduced Lunacy, is that it's a feat facilitated by proximity to the fetish-brick Ziggurat - a working of magic against the nature of the Uratha that would be considered blasphemous by the post-Oath Forsaken.<br /> <br /> So it wouldn't apply in the wilderness beyond Bau or any similar settlements.<br /> <br /> I wonder what Bau's relations with Kish are like...</div> </div> </div> </div>On a semi-related note, I wonder when exactly the Uratha would have regained Luna's favor and their Auspices. Part of me thinks that it could have happened sometime after the fall of the Nameless Empire, but it's not until after the conquest of Bau that the Oath of the Moon may have started to be ingrained into Forsaken ideology.<br /> <br /> Then, there's the matter of working out the lot of Werewolves in the Black Land, though the idea that they may be organized around Anpu, Wepwawet, and the Arisen of Abdju gives us a good place to start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T19:06:48-07:00","id":876192,"title":"","content":"Added in Arcanist's write-up on the Awakened view of Seba to the main post, albeit with some proofreading done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T02:19:08-07:00","id":876387,"title":"","content":"Tinkering with the Aeons still. I think Aset's appearance as the Aeon of Time coincides with the Sothic Turn (as she is tied to Sopdet herself). Before her, Khonsu was the Aeon of Time, willing to gamble for days or years etc.<br /> <br /> The question is whether Khonsu, or a shadow of him, is still wandering the Anima Mundi, or if the Same Aeon just completely transformed. Maybe, you CAN still meet Khonsu, but he is a cast-off Ren, the Aeon of Time having adopted a new Ren.<br /> <br /> Sutekh (or the sliver of him that is the Aeon of Fate) isn't missing yet as he will be millennia in the future ala the To The Strongest description. Rather he is the inevitable cycle of doom laying siege to Queen Aset's palace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-28-2016, 05:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T02:38:00-07:00","id":876402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=876387#post876387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tinkering with the Aeons still. I think Aset's appearance as the Aeon of Time coincides with the Sothic Turn (as she is tied to Sopdet herself). Before her, Khonsu was the Aeon of Time, willing to gamble for days or years etc.<br /> <br /> The question is whether Khonsu, or a shadow of him, is still wandering the Anima Mundi, or if the Same Aeon just completely transformed. Maybe, you CAN still meet Khonsu, but he is a cast-off Ren, the Aeon of Time having adopted a new Ren.<br /> <br /> Sutekh (or the sliver of him that is the Aeon of Fate) isn't missing yet as he will be millennia in the future ala the To The Strongest description. Rather he is the inevitable cycle of doom laying siege to Queen Aset's palace.</div> </div> </div> </div>That bit with Aset and Khonsu would be quite the Mystery, indeed. And I do wonder what would cause Sutek to disappear by Alexander's time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T07:30:03-07:00","id":876614,"title":"","content":"Remember that these are the Egyptian gods (sorta). The gods of syncretism (however it's spelt). Different gods, merging, splitting, trading aspects is completely appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T20:50:36-07:00","id":877286,"title":"","content":"I really like the idea of the blessings of the Uratha of Bau are due to the Fetish Ziggurat. It would probably be centred on a Locus for maximum effect. If they performed a version of the Wellspring Rite frequently, I could see the Uratha of Bau being even more powerful than they are already presented as.<br /> <br /> I did a little digging, and it appears as though &quot;Bau&quot; is the city of Isin, whose patron goddess was dog/wolf - headed and was sometimes called Bau. It was miles away from Kish, but only 20 miles away from Nippur, a major settlement. Its independence eventually collapsed and they became part of the realm of Uruk. Kish almost certainly dealt more with Babylon itself than it did Isin. I'll likely take a stab at some fluff once I do some more research.<br /> <br /> The bits about the Aeons are incredible. I love the idea of finding Khonsu somewhere out in the skies of the Anima Mundi, perhaps by way of speaking to the Goetic Anpu in Death's Temenos realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T22:15:47-07:00","id":877348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=877286#post877286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the idea of the blessings of the Uratha of Bau are due to the Fetish Ziggurat. It would probably be centred on a Locus for maximum effect. If they performed a version of the Wellspring Rite frequently, I could see the Uratha of Bau being even more powerful than they are already presented as.<br /> <br /> I did a little digging, and it appears as though &quot;Bau&quot; is the city of Isin, whose patron goddess was dog/wolf - headed and was sometimes called Bau. It was miles away from Kish, but only 20 miles away from Nippur, a major settlement. Its independence eventually collapsed and they became part of the realm of Uruk. Kish almost certainly dealt more with Babylon itself than it did Isin. I'll likely take a stab at some fluff once I do some more research.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ooooo... That's good to know! These are very basic so far, but may also be of of help: <br /> <br /> The Cannibal Hymn<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://orig13.deviantart.net/a6af/f/2016/119/2/f/cannibal_hymn_timeline_by_peace__out-da0q1fd.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><a href=\"http://orig13.deviantart.net/a6af/f/2016/119/2/f/cannibal_hymn_timeline_by_peace__out-da0q1fd.png\" target=\"_blank\">http://orig13.deviantart.net/a6af/f/...ut-da0q1fd.png</a><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Wolves of Ur-Sag<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px