eral) for the documents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T01:36:25-07:00","id":877462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=877348#post877348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wolves of Ur-Sag<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://orig02.deviantart.net/ba34/f/2016/119/0/e/wolves_of_ur_sag_timeline_by_peace__out-da0q1pw.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <a href=\"http://orig02.deviantart.net/ba34/f/2016/119/0/e/wolves_of_ur_sag_timeline_by_peace__out-da0q1pw.png\" target=\"_blank\">http://orig02.deviantart.net/ba34/f/...ut-da0q1pw.png</a></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Here's a useful Mummy relevant tidbit that I just stumbled across playing with some era ideas - this window for Ur-Sag aligns very neatly with the First Intermediate Period in Egypt, with the collapse of the Memphis Dynasty, and political chaos with temple desecrations with the rise rival dynasties in Upper and Lower Egypt. In other words, the exact type of thing that tends to result in either ambitious/defensive cults or tomb violations waking up the Arisen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-29-2016, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T09:05:21-07:00","id":878778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=877462#post877462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a useful Mummy relevant tidbit that I just stumbled across playing with some era ideas - this window for Ur-Sag aligns very neatly with the First Intermediate Period in Egypt, with the collapse of the Memphis Dynasty, and political chaos with temple desecrations with the rise rival dynasties in Upper and Lower Egypt. In other words, the exact type of thing that tends to result in either ambitious/defensive cults or tomb violations waking up the Arisen.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, if I get this right, Egypt would be in a state of civil war (with Arisen and Shuankhsen active at this time) while the Ur-Sag are active in Bau. It definitely makes me wonder if any of the trouble in the former were to turn up at the latter's doorstep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T03:39:46-07:00","id":879422,"title":"","content":"Quick question for everyone, with regard to Werewolves. Should the Tribes as we know them already be in existence by the time of the First Sothic Turn? I'm asking, since the general consensus here is that the Oath of the Moon came to be sometime after the Ur-Sag were toppled from power.<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, I'll be adding <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1isE4Wt_J7xLGB5a-6G-yI2j0DP36j_tIz-50kJAq_MM/edit\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> to the main post. Not sure if I've allowed for comments to be written in this, yet. But if that's the case, I'll fix that soon enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T14:34:29-07:00","id":879692,"title":"","content":"I'm in favor of no Tribes yet, but some Lodges can foreshadow them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T17:30:05-07:00","id":879791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=879692#post879692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm in favor of no Tribes yet, but some Lodges can foreshadow them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noted. How about Auspices? Should they have reappeared, by this point? Maybe during the expansion of the Nameless Empire or something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T18:57:39-07:00","id":879839,"title":"","content":"IF Auspices disappeared with the Sundering, they wouldn't return till the Oaths of the Moon, and mechanically during this window the Uratha would effectively all be Tribeless Pure.<br /> <br /> That's a big if though. It's possible they didn't lose Auspices at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T22:03:51-07:00","id":879909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=879839#post879839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IF Auspices disappeared with the Sundering, they wouldn't return till the Oaths of the Moon, and mechanically during this window the Uratha would effectively all be Tribeless Pure.<br /> <br /> That's a big if though. It's possible they didn't lose Auspices at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'd go with Auspices being around for Werewolves, more or less. But I wouldn't mind entertaining the possibility that they were lost, at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T23:26:31-07:00","id":879936,"title":"","content":"OH! IDEA!<br /> <br /> What if in this era, the default condition of Uratha is to be Auspice-less, BUT there is a rite that is circulating (and feared) that allows a werewolf to rededicate themselves to the Moon, and assume an Auspice. The Oaths of the Moon is something that happened gradually, not all at once!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T02:41:01-07:00","id":880001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=879936#post879936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OH! IDEA!<br /> <br /> What if in this era, the default condition of Uratha is to be Auspice-less, BUT there is a rite that is circulating (and feared) that allows a werewolf to rededicate themselves to the Moon, and assume an Auspice. The Oaths of the Moon is something that happened gradually, not all at once!</div> </div> </div> </div>.... Actually <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Maybe <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/760666-2ed-your-s-werewolf-rites#post760666\">this</a> could be the rite responsible for the Uratha reclaiming their Auspices? This idea first started off from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=750787#post750787\">this initial version</a>, and then it was gradually streamlined with further revisions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T03:26:44-07:00","id":880014,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... there should be something fundamentally frightening about it I think.... wait... hold on, I deleted what I said before on this post, because I think I have a better idea, hold on. I'm tinkering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T17:47:41-07:00","id":880611,"title":"","content":"So, Mage is out on Wednesday. I fully intend on grabbing hold of it, plunging headfirst, and really digging in to what makes the Awakened of Kemet tick.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, I'm still pondering over how to handle the Lodges of Kemet. Wepwawet is almost <i>definitely </i>the Totem of one, but I'm not entirely sure what kind of patron they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T18:02:35-07:00","id":880622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=880611#post880611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Mage is out on Wednesday. I fully intend on grabbing hold of it, plunging headfirst, and really digging in to what makes the Awakened of Kemet tick.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, I'm still pondering over how to handle the Lodges of Kemet. Wepwawet is almost <i>definitely </i>the Totem of one, but I'm not entirely sure what kind of patron they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm also wondering how the Arisen-guided Lodge would work. Part of me was thinking that the 'Totem' might have something to do with an Omphalos Stone somehow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T18:11:03-07:00","id":880631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=880622#post880622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm also wondering how the Arisen-guided Lodge would work. Part of me was thinking that the 'Totem' might have something to do with an Omphalos Stone somehow?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's an independent Lodge, I'd definitely call for Wepawet as patron, assuming the Forsaken on Kemet don't already use him as another name for Father Wolf. As for a Lodge operating as an Arisen cult, it's much more likely to be one dedicated to the most important canone in Irem; Anpu. Hell, they could very easily be a proto-Eaters of the Dead aimed at hunting Lifeless monstrosities and aimed at the Shuankhsen infesting the Black Land in this era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T18:31:25-07:00","id":880643,"title":"","content":"It's entirely possible that Wepwawet is the Kemetic name for Father Wolf, but I'm rather fond of the idea of them being a Lodge patron that can be interacted with. I love the idea of the Abdju Lodge being early Eaters of the Dead. They might not even be tied to a Spirit with Anpu's image, but Anpu himself. He is running around Neter-Khteret afterall.<br /> <br /> Ooh, now I'm picturing a pack of the Abdju Lodge with one or more sha as packmates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T03:21:05-07:00","id":880844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=880643#post880643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's entirely possible that Wepwawet is the Kemetic name for Father Wolf, but I'm rather fond of the idea of them being a Lodge patron that can be interacted with. I love the idea of the Abdju Lodge being early Eaters of the Dead. They might not even be tied to a Spirit with Anpu's image, but Anpu himself. He is running around Neter-Khteret afterall.<br /> <br /> Ooh, now I'm picturing a pack of the Abdju Lodge with one or more sha as packmates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of Sha, were there ever any mechanics and/or stats for them? I assume they're going to be some sort of Ephemeral Being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T15:26:22-07:00","id":881304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=880844#post880844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking of Sha, were there ever any mechanics and/or stats for them? I assume they're going to be some sort of Ephemeral Being.</div> </div> </div> </div>They had a full statblock in Sothis Ascends. They're corporeal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T17:22:57-07:00","id":881374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=881304#post881304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They had a full statblock in Sothis Ascends. They're corporeal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Thanks.<br /> <br /> Say, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a>, could you post that Uter made by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1059\" data-vbnamecard=\"1059\">Azahul</a> here, if you can? The one that you said could be used to make Apep Materialize in all his glorious horror?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T09:34:39-07:00","id":881905,"title":"","content":"Have we discussed Changeling here at all? I was pondering this recently and had a couple of ideas to toss against the wall.<br /> <br /> We have this concept of traversing the Hedge and getting into the far realm of the Others. We also have this notion in several ancient mythologies that the seats of the divine was real physical places that could be reached by semi-divine or even purely mortal beings. I think it would be interesting to incorporate this and reimagine how Durances work in this distant era. By way of rough example, I have a couple of alternative Seeming concepts.<br /> <br /> <b>Habbatu</b> - One who was gained entrance to the fae lands through stealth. Stealing into the abode of gods and monsters to retrieve something of value in their Durance. This could be a legendary treasure, secret wisdom, or even a person. They have returned to the mortal world with the object of their desire, but stealing from the gods always carries a cost.<br /> <br /> Blessing: A powerful item (three dot Token) or a spirit familiar (three dot Retainer) which is bound to them and can never be permanently lost.<br /> <br /> Curse: The Others have spread far and wide that the Habbatu are thieves and not to be trusted. Purchasing dots in Contracts costs and additional Experience as spirits are reluctant to enter into agreements with them.<br /> <br /> <b>Nakru</b> - A child of the fae lands who has been sent to be raised in the world of men. Always apart from their surroundings by dint of their divine heritage and mortal upbringing theirs is a Durance which never truly ends. They possess the power of the distant Others but are forever marked by it.<br /> <br /> Blessing: Legendary Prowess. One attribute chosen at creation which gains the 9-again quality.<br /> <br /> Curse: There is forever a strangeness about them that mortals can sense and which the fae are repelled by. They have a -2 penalty on rolls of social skills against mortals and denizens of Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T16:45:47-07:00","id":882342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=881905#post881905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have we discussed Changeling here at all? I was pondering this recently and had a couple of ideas to toss against the wall.<br /> <br /> We have this concept of traversing the Hedge and getting into the far realm of the Others. We also have this notion in several ancient mythologies that the seats of the divine was real physical places that could be reached by semi-divine or even purely mortal beings. I think it would be interesting to incorporate this and reimagine how Durances work in this distant era. By way of rough example, I have a couple of alternative Seeming concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have been thinking of starting some ideas for Changelings, but refrained from doing so until all the Changeling 2E material is out. That said, those alternative Seemings seem promising, but their write-ups are still more 1E than 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T16:58:54-07:00","id":882352,"title":"","content":"So a question we'd have to answer with Changeling: does the Contract of Iron break with the first time a human forges iron (in which case it's already happened at this point), or does it not count until the technology develops and spreads allowing a true iron age to begin (still almost a millennium away)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T22:21:38-07:00","id":882570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=881374#post881374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah. Thanks.<br /> <br /> Say, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a>, could you post that Uter made by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1059\" data-vbnamecard=\"1059\">Azahul</a> here, if you can? The one that you said could be used to make Apep Materialize in all his glorious horror?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be curious to see this too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T23:37:10-07:00","id":882615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=882570#post882570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be curious to see this too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. And as was mentioned earlier in this thread, a Materialized Rank 6 monster like Apep would be the centerpiece in a chronicle's climax.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T05:12:48-07:00","id":882786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=882615#post882615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. And as was mentioned earlier in this thread, a Materialized Rank 6 monster like Apep would be the centerpiece in a chronicle's climax.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just not sure that I ever wrote something like that. I did have an Ephemeral Entity in my Mummy chronicle called the Coils of Apep, but it was a minion of a separate entity which was bound to a 5 dot Seba. Not sure which Uter you might be talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T05:56:37-07:00","id":882800,"title":"","content":"The World's Wound, which crushed Neter-Khetet and the physical world together, is the one I was thinking of. It was the effect of ripping down Twilight that made me think it could, potentially, force Apep to materialize in the Flesh as opposed to sending a Royal Avatar or being pursued into the Shadow. My logic was that it would temporarily warp the area into a Verge.<br /> <br /> Here's the Relic in question, as written by you.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/216621-old-gods-of-jakarta-mummy-actual-play?p=619562#post619562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The World\u2019s Wound (5 dot Bane Uter)<br /> <br /> <i>The World\u2019s Wound appears as nothing more than a pile of decaying viscera. Attempts to examine it find that it appears to be from a mix of different animals, strangely fused together during decomposition. The smell coming from the mouldering flesh is disturbing, but worse are the sensations conjured up through proximity to the Uter. It mixes lust and hunger in equal measure, an appalling desire for more. What it is that the watcher craves isn\u2019t clear, even to them, but it can drive them to commit the basest of acts in an attempt to fulfil it.</i><br /> <i>Whenever the World\u2019s Wound is moved, a gruesome task by any measure, those who examine the ground where it rested find trails of black and red gore laid out in the shape of spidery runes. They seem to swim and shift before the eyes of the onlooker, but their shapes sear themselves into the memory of those who witness them. Although they write in no language ever spoken by mortal men, all who see them know they promise madness and the death of all things.</i><br /> <br /> Power: The World\u2019s Wound tears the line between reality and unreality, forcing space and time and the otherworld that is Neter-Khetet to bleed together. But before it can rend the laws of the universe so thoroughly, it requires a sacrifice. Forty-two innocents (defined as anyone of Morality 7 or higher) must be sacrificed to the Wound in order to activate its power. The blood of these sacrifices seep into the Wound\u2019s rotten flesh, and a spectral wail can be heard as their souls are condemned to an eternity of agony.<br /> The Wound\u2019s power creeps forth with the death of the final sacrifice. It claims the site of the sacrifice as its domain. The definition of a \u201csite\u201d is arcane, but generally it is along the lines of a large building and surrounding grounds, or an arbitrary amount of land of approximately equal size. Mortals are driven from the area in fear, and from that point forward they will be unable to notice or enter the site of their own free will. Anything that takes place there will go unseen by onlookers, even if the chosen site is an open field. Witnesses and those with an appropriate Unseen Sense feel revulsion and horror from proximity to the area.<br /> For supernatural beings, they see a strange shimmer when looking at the area of influence from the outside. It makes the area appear to be a mirage. It is hard to focus upon, and bringing oneself to believe that there is something of note there is quite hard without knowing of the relic\u2019s existence.<br /> Inside the bounds of the relic\u2019s influence, the world is broken. The state of Twilight seems to cease to exist, causing Amkhata and ghosts inside the area to be manifested physically. The manifestation modifier of the area rises to +5, overriding any other effects that may alter it.<br /> The corruption bleeding from the Wound alters the nature of the surrounding area in a variety of other unpredictable ways. Cracks in walls reveal pulsating, infected flesh, weeping trickles of blood. The view through windows shows unfamiliar stars in a strangely discoloured sky, mottled purple like a bruise. It alters the layout of buildings and leads to twisted and alien architecture that defies reason, from vaulted halls built for colossal beings of inhuman biology to tunnels that burrow through the walls and twist in on themselves endlessly.<br /> The Wound seeks to protect the one who performed the sacrifice, and intruders can be subjected to any one of a different number of effects. These range from visions and illusions, the creation of demons and strange spirits to destroy intruders, or attempts by the very land itself to elimate the intruder. Treat it like Retributive Curse\u2019s narrative level obstacle, except that whatever obstacle is chosen should have a good chance of killing the intruder. Each intruder who comes with ill-intent towards the one who performed the sacrifice triggers an obstacle of their own, although an individual obstacle may be dangerous enough to destroy every such attacker at once should they enter as a group.<br /> Utterances and other magic unleashed within the bounds of this territory can only affect the territory, their effects do not go beyond and remain unnoticed by any potential onlookers.<br /> This relic cannot be drained for Sekhem.<br /> <br /> Curse: The Wound feeds on the Sekhem of the surrounding area. This has a corrupting effect on mortals, causing them to sicken and die in droves. For regular mortals, this could be mistaken for a minor outbreak of a serious disease, from malaria to pneumonia. It strikes randomly, and its effects are usually survivable.<br /> The exceptions are those mortals who have been touched by Irem. Witnesses are almost certain to die, some dropping from heart attacks after prolonged exposure to the relic\u2019s influence (spending more than a week within a mile radius of its location). Next are the Cultists, who will be guaranteed to be infected by the disease. Individuals who have had other contact, particularly being subjected to Sybaris, simply have a higher rate of infection.<br /> The exact impact of this curse\u2019s effects on individual NPCs is up to the Storyteller. As a rule, all cults within ten miles lose a dot of Reach or Grasp every month. The plague may spread further than that, carried in the water, in vermin, or by the diseased themselves, but will have a lesser impact on cults outside of the region.<br /> The cultists of Shuankhsen are immune to this Curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T06:57:27-07:00","id":882829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=882342#post882342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have been thinking of starting some ideas for Changelings, but refrained from doing so until all the Changeling 2E material is out. That said, those alternative Seemings seem promising, but their write-ups are still more 1E than 2E.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true. I haven't had the chance to really digest the 2E spoilers we've gotten so I'm spit-balling based on the edition I know. The slap dash write up was just trying to demonstrate the idea I was going for with each of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T13:36:07-07:00","id":883178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=882800#post882800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The World's Wound, which crushed Neter-Khetet and the physical world together, is the one I was thinking of. It was the effect of ripping down Twilight that made me think it could, potentially, force Apep to materialize in the Flesh as opposed to sending a Royal Avatar or being pursued into the Shadow. My logic was that it would temporarily warp the area into a Verge.<br /> <br /> Here's the Relic in question, as written by you.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah, that one. Very true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T17:24:40-07:00","id":884172,"title":"","content":"So. Revisiting how Mage Sight interacts with Seba now that the Mage 2E stuff is out....<br /> <br /> Fate Sight should allow one to perceive Seba (and the creation of those of the artistic variety), whereas Active Time Sight would show the signs of an active (or even approaching) convergence event. That seems to be something all of us can agree on. The question, though, is this... Would Active Mage Sight be enough? Or would a Mage need to use Focused Mage Sight to see them.<br /> <br /> And how about other types of Mage Sight? I'm still open to the idea that Prime Sight can also allow for perception of Seba, seeing as the Arcanum's capabilities include being able to pierce illusions. And seeing as Prime's purviews include truth and revelation, that also makes sense. Even so, I can see this requiring Focused Mage Sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T18:31:30-07:00","id":884225,"title":"","content":"So I'm kind of thinking that the rite that restores Auspice should actually tend to leave recipiants moon-mad. Their descendants who get their Auspice on their First Change (barring a Pure blocking rite) don't have this problem, but those who chose to rededicate themselves to the Warding Moon are left a deranged - a trade off for the power boost of Auspice. This contributes to why the rite is so feared despite its obvious attached power.<br /> <br /> It's also mutually exclusive with the enhanced self-control, and decreased Lunacy, provided by the Fetish Ziggurat as in Bau.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T22:38:45-07:00","id":884395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=884225#post884225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm kind of thinking that the rite that restores Auspice should actually tend to leave recipiants moon-mad. Their descendants who get their Auspice on their First Change (barring a Pure blocking rite) don't have this problem, but those who chose to rededicate themselves to the Warding Moon are left a deranged - a trade off for the power boost of Auspice. This contributes to why the rite is so feared despite its obvious attached power.<br /> <br /> It's also mutually exclusive with the enhanced self-control, and decreased Lunacy, provided by the Fetish Ziggurat as in Bau.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps that Rite could be an early and imperfect precursor to the Luna's Forgiveness Rite I posted sometime before?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T19:51:36-07:00","id":885113,"title":"","content":"I have added a link to my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1C_5xgAlNHHnXKnShladcn_r_tBLDclHhbmALEr4fgnw/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">Neferi Bloodline</a> on the main post. To those who haven't yet read them, they are a Mekhet Bloodline associated with the mortal Temple of Silence, but who are assumed (by default) to have gone extinct by modern nights. They also have a (hinted) connection along blood ties to another Bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T07:08:42-07:00","id":889084,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I forgot that the Abyss was associated with the Primordial Waters. May need to rethink the Stygian Aeons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T14:41:46-07:00","id":889366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=854199#post854199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bAs a heads-up, Upuaut/Wepwawet has some coverage in The Pack.<br /> <br /> \u200bEdit: It's just a little bit of coverage. But if you want to know it sooner rather than later, ask Stew to reveal the Lodge of Garm write-up on the blog post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And The Pack is now out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T16:35:22-07:00","id":889452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=889366#post889366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And The Pack is now out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, can <i>someone</i> post that tidbit on Wepwawet that Acro mentioned much earlier in this thread? I am dying to know more here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T18:27:55-07:00","id":889522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=889452#post889452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, can <i>someone</i> post that tidbit on Wepwawet that Acro mentioned much earlier in this thread? I am dying to know more here.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just brief, but Upuaut is one of the names that Gram Wolf, the son of Destroyer Wolf and totem of the Lodge of Garm is known by. The Garmir are basically the Blood Talons of the Blood Talons, they don't just hunt other Werewolves, but the specialize in Werewolves with high Primal Urge. They also have the unwitting aspiration to be defeated by superior foes, which is very interesting in the context of facing the Arisen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T20:20:31-07:00","id":889590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=889522#post889522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's just brief, but Upuaut is one of the names that Gram Wolf, the son of Destroyer Wolf and totem of the Lodge of Garm is known by. The Garmir are basically the Blood Talons of the Blood Talons, they don't just hunt other Werewolves, but the specialize in Werewolves with high Primal Urge. They also have the unwitting aspiration to be defeated by superior foes, which is very interesting in the context of facing the Arisen.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Arisen... or Apep. It's interesting that they're called out as, essentially, the bloodiest of Blood Talons. Though I could have sworn reading elsewhere that the Garmir are the Eaters of the Dead, or are they a different Lodge?<br /> <br /> Either way, there are four definite Lodges operating in this time and place. The Eaters of the Dead, the Garmir, the Abdju Lodge dedicated to Anpu, and the lords of Bau who might be heirs of the Tyrants and/or the Shepherds from the Sundered World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T21:06:22-07:00","id":889620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=889590#post889590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Arisen... or Apep. It's interesting that they're called out as, essentially, the bloodiest of Blood Talons. Though I could have sworn reading elsewhere that the Garmir are the Eaters of the Dead, or are they a different Lodge?<br /> <br /> Either way, there are four definite Lodges operating in this time and place. The Eaters of the Dead, the Garmir, the Abdju Lodge dedicated to Anpu, and the lords of Bau who might be heirs of the Tyrants and/or the Shepherds from the Sundered World.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I think I missed something...Where did the Eaters of the Dead come from? My understanding is that they are Central Asin and relatively recent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T21:22:06-07:00","id":889625,"title":"","content":"I'll admit that I'm not exactly up to snuff on Lodges and Werewolf Lore, so I'm probably more or less entirely wrong. I think something like the Eaters of the Dead are necessary though, what with all the Lifeless running around. The Abdju Lodge would probably work well for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T21:42:47-07:00","id":889638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=889590#post889590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Arisen... or Apep. It's interesting that they're called out as, essentially, the bloodiest of Blood Talons. Though I could have sworn reading elsewhere that the Garmir are the Eaters of the Dead, or are they a different Lodge?<br /> <br /> Either way, there are four definite Lodges operating in this time and place. The Eaters of the Dead, the Garmir, the Abdju Lodge dedicated to Anpu, and the lords of Bau who might be heirs of the Tyrants and/or the Shepherds from the Sundered World.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Eaters of the Dead are definitely not the Lodge of Garm and are a recent group of Ghost Wolves originally out of Mongolia who happen to think they've found a long-lost Firstborn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T22:23:52-07:00","id":889658,"title":"","content":"Yup, my Lodge-fu is weak. Good to have the confirmation. I can definitely see the Abdju Lodge fulfilling a similar function though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T23:30:07-07:00","id":889695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=889658#post889658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup, my Lodge-fu is weak. Good to have the confirmation. I can definitely see the Abdju Lodge fulfilling a similar function though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted, the Eaters of the Dead are born from the discovery of a long-dead (or for our purposes, let's claim mummified) potential Firstborn. It could very well be that their patron, Ravening Wolf, was up and about leading packs in a glorious hunt against the undead; she has three thiusand years to wind up in Mongolia, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T22:24:53-07:00","id":890997,"title":"","content":"Quick thought on the Anima Mundi - the &quot;four domains&quot; model uses Egyptian names but is clearly based on the Greek division of the Elements. I propose instead the Weret-Hekau in this era make no distinction between the Earth Domain and the Domain of Heat - both are Just different parts of the body of Keb. Then what future Mages will call Neut the Sky Domain, the Old Kingdom Egyptian Mages identify as Shu - the body of Air between Earth and Heaven. Neut in turn is how they identify the Sidereal Wastes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T07:01:15-07:00","id":902017,"title":"","content":"Inspired by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a>' write-up for the Purified in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a>'s Sundered World Chronicles thread. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> also gets a mention due to some of the text alluding to some of his stuff. <hr /><br /> \u200b<b><u>Purified in the Black Land</u></b><br /> <br /> As a source of one of the oldest written records on the magics which create Purified, Kemet was home to a considerable number of these Immortals. Ancient Egyptian mummification was clearly derived from a form of the ritual for purification, but was a debased and fruitless process that did nothing more than preserve the corpse. This was because almost all of the ancient Egyptian Purified were priests and magicians who reserved the accurate techniques for themselves and a few of their most favored acolytes and companions.<br /> <br /> In the Black Land, both the inner and outer paths of purifications are pursued by those seeking immortality. And the Purified are a discrete yet influential minority among its shadowy denizens. Stories and theories exist in this era on their nature and origins, and circulate among both mundane and supernatural circles. What those tales are, though, depend on who is the one doing the talking.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Chosen of Old Gods</b><br /> <i>&quot;The story is true. Once, men and women journeyed from the villages of the People into the furthest reaches of Pangaea. Like the Wise Ones, they sought out the gods for power. Yet unlike them, they did not wish to take their hearts from their defiled corpses. Those who earned their favor were bestowed great gifts, becoming their heralds and champions in the two worlds. Few of these Wanderers survived the loss of our paradise. But they walk among us, still.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Not enough time has passed yet to distort the tales of the Asilal-thakh, the &quot;Distant Wanderers&quot;. And the Uratha have managed to preserve most beyond the passing of those who would come to be called the Vinca. They remember how some of the mortal herd ventured on pilgrimages to the Border Marches, to seek out and commune with the gods who dwelled within. Most are never seen again, but those who succeeded would return to the People with a god of Pangaea as their totem.<br /> <br /> When the Sundering came, however, the Wanderers suffered just as the Uratha and the Wise did. Most were crippled as they found themselves separated from their patrons by the rising Gauntlet. Others were less fortunate, as the barrier destroyed those Pangaeans who failed to escape to either world for one reason or another. A majority of these immortals die on the spot, or otherwise go insane without a proper channel for the powers they wielded.<br /> <br /> Like other survivors of Pangaea's destruction, however, the Returned adapt. Many would shed one aspect of their nature to cope, just as the Pangaeans they served did the same. Those who severed their ties to the conceptual heart of the world became more akin to denizens of the Shadow. Their powers were diminished somewhat, but they were still as undying as the spirits were.<br /> <br /> In time, these immortals would find their place in the new world. And they would soon be joined by others, those who discovered new avenues to achieving immortality. These individuals would pioneer the first practices that would form the inner and outer paths of purification, and would thus give rise to the contemporary term of Purified.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Returned from Neter-Khertet</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;Many of the Empire's secrets remain lost beneath the sands. But the desert always yields them to those declared worthy by the gods. However, this has not stopped others less deserving from seeking out the relics. And we may have lost what may be the crowning glory of the old kings to such thieves. Why do I tell you this? Turn your sight upon that priest, my child. Do you notice how he carries the weight of so many years despite his youth? Focus, now, and see him for what he truly is.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The sorcerers of the Weret-Hekau consider it their duty to uncover, preserve, and (if necessary) destroy the works of the Predynastic ancients. But they accept with trepidation that they are not the only ones who have successfully harnessed the wonders of their kingdom's mythical past. And some of those they compete with claim to have greater rights over the Nameless Empire's relics by virtue of the fact that they had lived at the height of its glory.<br /> <br /> Few Hemka have successful dealings with them. Those men and women who live through countless flood cycles, yet never grow old even as their minds grow wiser with age. They are believed to be the custodians of Irem's greatest - and most dangerous - sorcery, which was said to make mortals ascend to become divinities unto themselves. That these people are undying by nature leads many Awakened to believe that they claimed this secret for themselves, and only share it to those they deem worthy.<br /> <br /> Among the Priests of the Fivefold Soul, it is those who made their decree to the Ab who are perhaps best equipped to deal with the Returned. Like them, they deal frequently with the demons and minor gods that populate the Neter-Khertet, and that the strongest of those entities maintain alliances with several of these Undying Ones. Such alliances, and the fact that the Undying themselves have powers of their own, have kept the Hemka from probing deeply into their affairs. And, more than once, this has even led to hostilities breaking out between members of both societies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Heretics of the Nameless Empire</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;Our rebellion was not the first heresy to plague the Empire. Other gods worked from the shadows to spread their influence among the slaves, and perhaps even into the halls of the Guilds. And they, too, had prophets of their own. Men and women who claimed to have been alive before the first pillars were raised. They preached that their gods once walked among the mortals, and that they may do so again if the people raised their voices in praise to them. The Shan'iatu punished those prophets as brutally as they did our own. But many of them managed to swim against the River's flow to return and continue their masters' work.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Even at the height of their power, Irem was still plagued from within by practices its rulers considered taboo. The Cult of the Crocodile God and the White Rebellion were some of the most notable of these dissenters, but many other voices rang in opposition to the hymns of the Judges. The leaders of some of these heresies were witches, occult practitioners who learned to harness the Essence of the soul through blasphemous rituals.<br /> <br /> These heathens were hunted down by the Shan'iatu whenever they banded together. But it was those witches who were favored by the demons living in Neter-Khertet who were counted among their greatest adversaries. Some of these individuals are even blessed with immortality by their patrons, and could return from Duat so long as their souls were not sundered outside their bodies.<br /> <br /> In the days of the Old Kingdom, some Hemka and other lesser scholars who have searched for a connection between the Returned and the Nameless Empire come to believe that the rituals and practices used by the former may have stemmed from the latter's experiments with Sekhem. A small minoriy, however, theorize that it was the reverse. The first iterations of what will come to be called the inner and outer paths of purification may have been appropriated by the Scorpion Kings, and repurposed by them to manipulate instead the true lifeblood of the cosmos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T11:54:27-07:00","id":902192,"title":"","content":"So. On a more Awakened note, any plans on reskinning the Darshanas to better reflect the cultures highlighted in the setting? For starters, we do have a rough idea on how to flesh them out from a Kemetic perspective based on what was written in To the Strongest.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Jnanashakti/Mysterium:</b> &quot;Egyptian Sebau (singular, Seba) take their names from the class of scribes. They preserve ancient knowledge given by the gods, even if they have to plunder old tombs to do it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Mahanizrayani/Silver Ladder: </b>&quot;Egyptian Tjati act as priest\u2013viziers to the ruling class. They believe worthy rulers are manifestations of the gods, and are determined to make sure they act that way.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Samashti/Guardians of the Veil:</b> &quot;The Egyptian Sepermeru (\u201cnear to the desert\u201d) cult follows Set, the sinister god of storms and strangers who nonetheless serves by battling Apep, serpent of chaos.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Vajrastra/Adamantine Arrow:</b> &quot;The Weret-Hekau call their protectors Medjay, after Egypt\u2019s Nubian warrior elite. &quot;<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> That leaves us with the equivalent of Ajivaki and Libertines for Age of Azar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T14:53:55-07:00","id":902298,"title":"","content":"The concept of Darshanas don't exist yet. You're just going to have factions like the Tjati and the Sepermeru. The Medjay are definitely anachronistic for the Old Kingdom and need to be replaced. I'll dig a bit on the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T15:14:10-07:00","id":902308,"title":"","content":"I'm actually inclined to reverse the Sebau and the Sepermeru in the Old Kingdom, to emphasize how the factions have evolved by the time you get to the dawn of the Hellenistic Age.<br /> <br /> The Sebau won't be a guild of scribes until the New Kingdom. Instead in this era they are harsh teachers (the word &quot;seba&quot; means both teach and beat), and are closest to the Samashti role in the Great Cult.<br /> <br /> The doctrine of Sutekh that defines the Sepermeru in future ages is still being born at this point. Instead those &quot;near the desert&quot; are nomadic gatherers of stories, knowledge, and mysteries, coming closest to the Jnanashakti role in the Cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T18:14:05-07:00","id":903153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=902308#post902308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually inclined to reverse the Sebau and the Sepermeru in the Old Kingdom, to emphasize how the factions have evolved by the time you get to the dawn of the Hellenistic Age.<br /> <br /> The Sebau won't be a guild of scribes until the New Kingdom. Instead in this era they are harsh teachers (the word &quot;seba&quot; means both teach and beat), and are closest to the Samashti role in the Great Cult.<br /> <br /> The doctrine of Sutekh that defines the Sepermeru in future ages is still being born at this point. Instead those &quot;near the desert&quot; are nomadic gatherers of stories, knowledge, and mysteries, coming closest to the Jnanashakti role in the Cult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I can work with this. Now, we just need to put it to a write-up in the main document for the Mage section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T23:01:41-07:00","id":903286,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a>. Anything yet on a term for those closest to the Vajrastra darshana in Age of Azar? I've managed to write down some text on the Tjati, Sebau, and Sepermeru for the First Sothic Turn, and added it to the GDoc. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Tjati act as priest\u2013viziers to the ruling class. They believe worthy rulers are manifestations of the gods, and are determined to make sure they act that way. As a result, these Hemka readily embrace their purpose as guides and luminaries, emulating Imhotep\u2019s example by inspiring the Pharaoh and the people to greater heights.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sebau are harsh teachers. They instruct other sorcerers to honor Ma'at in their duties, but also carry the duty of hunting down those who have strayed from that obligation. A sorcerer must strive towards a life of balance, they say, lest he be punished by the gods in this life. And should he fail to seek proper penance, his judgement is forfeit, and his soul is condemned to the jaws of Ammut as soon as it passes into Duat.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There are some Hemka who choose to distance themselves from the people, and instead devote their time in the pursuit of ancient and forgotten lore. T</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">hese sorcerers dwell near the desert, where they roam as nomadic gatherers of stories, knowledge, and mysteries. It is they who pioneer the growth of their tradition, as many of the Weret-Hekau's</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> discoveries on the Nameless Empire were made by these intrepid seekers.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T23:28:26-07:00","id":903295,"title":"","content":"How about &quot;Mehenw&quot;? If the Weret-Hekau was founded by Imhotep, they'd presumably have heavy Re symbology, and the serpent &quot;Mehen&quot; protects Re during the nightly battle with Apep. That battling-chaos concept would be powerful for the &quot;Coiled Ones&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T08:27:32-07:00","id":903559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=903295#post903295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about &quot;Mehenw&quot;? If the Weret-Hekau was founded by Imhotep, they'd presumably have heavy Re symbology, and the serpent &quot;Mehen&quot; protects Re during the nightly battle with Apep. That battling-chaos concept would be powerful for the &quot;Coiled Ones&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh. That actually works. Perhaps that could be a term used alongside &quot;Medjay&quot;, seeing as the actual Medjay form Kemet's military according to Sothis Ascends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T11:27:49-07:00","id":903676,"title":"","content":"In this era?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T16:15:25-07:00","id":903833,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sothis Ascends, pg. 23</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Medjay are famed archers and are found in large numbers in Upper Kemet, where they mostly find work as soldiers and bodyguards.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sothis Ascends, pg. 25</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Medjay are the ethnic group hailing from Ta-Seti, the foreign land bordering on Kemet\u2019s southern reaches. Large numbers of Medjay have entered Kemet over the centuries, and they maintain their own clans in and amongst the greater population. Medjay have no rights as citizens, though are still protected from wrongdoing by the law \u2014 they don\u2019t take part in civic labor, but aren\u2019t supported in hard times either, and must find work for themselves. Their people have a long martial tradition of their own, and as they don\u2019t work in other careers most of the year like Kemet\u2019s own citizen-soldiers, many Medjay find work as hunters, bodyguards, soldiers, and constables for local law enforcement. By the time of the Turn, the Medjay working for the nomarchs and Great House make up almost all of Kemet\u2019s tiny \u201cstanding army,\u201d and armed Medjay are an unremarkable sight in and around the nation\u2019s centers of power. Arisen who are ethnically \u201cNubian\u201d are usually seen as Medjay by mortals once their sahu fully forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T16:40:39-07:00","id":903848,"title":"","content":"Ok. I think some historians would dispute that confluence in the Old Kingdom, but if that's what they went with with the CoD take on the era than go with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T16:56:53-07:00","id":903853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=903848#post903848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. I think some historians would dispute that confluence in the Old Kingdom, but if that's what they went with with the CoD take on the era than go with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will do. Also added a GDoc that covers the general way of life for Kemet's people, lifted straight from Sothis Ascends. Will be adding original sections for the different supernatural splats sometime later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T05:38:07-07:00","id":904880,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19pettOSEIP7X6VjDx8pjjZ4LJyyCjLUuazTh3U80JDo/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Added a section</a> which discusses the major cities of Kemet. So far, the entry of Inbu-Hedj (Memphis) in Sothis Ascends is there, albeit with some additional points discussing other supernatural populations in the city. If any of you guys are interesting in adding more - or even covering other major cult centers, feel free to post your contributions here or suggest them on the GDoc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 06-01-2016, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T23:42:07-07:00","id":905432,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a>. Mentioning here since I was going through the &quot;Dominion of Re&quot; section in Sothis Ascends the other day. Going by <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GtkjmOolHZK_uYM3rjKG2-7UnN6kiX7vyTEtM5Ic8Jw/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#heading=h.8nixer5uywrm\" target=\"_blank\">your rules</a> for Unease Sybaris, the bonus provided by being in the proximity of Re's shrines and temples should translate to additional dice, yes?<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, and as a general question, what do you guys think of said temples and shrines acting as <i>very</i> potent Environmental Yantras for Awakened sorcerers of that era sworn to Re? I've been trying to figure out how to handle it. But so far, I was thinking of applying half their Sybaris bonus, rounded up, as additional dice to the spells which can be semiotically linked to them. Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T16:18:27-07:00","id":906041,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.madote.com/2010/03/land-of-punt-is-eritrea.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjtYsjCRvJ3aKmKLzfKtJ2_hqvtGfm0E6CVpHSb2PylXFfyVQ2K0CqVSWExwU98StnUQy22vVDIf59y3mwTbrjGk2ZyLrUNem5v3RZp27GMtskVLtndZy4aWoBa5V38S448GRPH-FCpIIw/w1200-h630-p-k-no-nu/Punt+people+2.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.madote.com/2010/03/land-of-punt-is-eritrea.html\" target=\"_blank\"> The Land of Punt is Eritrea </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.madote.com/2010/03/land-of-punt-is-eritrea.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.madote.com/2010/03/land-of-punt-is-eritrea.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Eritrean News and Views </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Might be relevant for your stuff on the Land of Punt. But that said, where did you place it as being located at when you were conceiving the Mumvuri?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T19:45:00-07:00","id":907392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=905432#post905432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a>. Mentioning here since I was going through the &quot;Dominion of Re&quot; section in Sothis Ascends the other day. Going by <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GtkjmOolHZK_uYM3rjKG2-7UnN6kiX7vyTEtM5Ic8Jw/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#heading=h.8nixer5uywrm\" target=\"_blank\">your rules</a> for Unease Sybaris, the bonus provided by being in the proximity of Re's shrines and temples should translate to additional dice, yes?<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, and as a general question, what do you guys think of said temples and shrines acting as <i>very</i> potent Environmental Yantras for Awakened sorcerers of that era sworn to Re? I've been trying to figure out how to handle it. But so far, I was thinking of applying half their Sybaris bonus, rounded up, as additional dice to the spells which can be semiotically linked to them. Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The bonus provided by being in proximity to Re's shrines should translate to additional dice. Also, if you actually <i>worship </i>at the shrine, consider keeping that bonus for a number of days equal to the rating of the bonus. This, of course, being cribbed from the Temple Merit from the Secrets of the Covenants spoilers, and which I adapted to my Cults for Everyone material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T21:06:09-07:00","id":907433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=907392#post907392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bonus provided by being in proximity to Re's shrines should translate to additional dice. Also, if you actually <i>worship </i>at the shrine, consider keeping that bonus for a number of days equal to the rating of the bonus. This, of course, being cribbed from the Temple Merit from the Secrets of the Covenants spoilers, and which I adapted to my Cults for Everyone material.</div> </div> </div> </div>So half the Sybaris bonus, rounded up, for being in proximity to a holy site of Re. And if a Mage actually worships at the shrine, the bonus is retained for a number of days equal to the full bonus? Hehe. This definitely puts the Awakened among the solar priesthood at a big advantage, especially when you consider the additional boost from having Status in Re's Cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T21:29:27-07:00","id":907438,"title":"","content":"A section to be filled out in its wn GDoc. Legacies. Some of these are familiar from previous books. Others are original concepts. <hr /><br /> <b><u>LEGACIES OF THE FIVEFOLD SOUL</u></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Ab</u></b><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Dreamspeakers:</b> All sorcerers can enter a state of mind which allows them to reach the fringes of A'aru. Those initiated into the Legacy are more skilled than most, with the greatest of their number able to cast their Ba to the stars while awake. When Sybaris shapes the dreams of certain mortals, these Hemka work to interpret the omens they bring. (Mind)<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Keepers of the Covenant:</b> More numerous in this age of gods, the Legacy's Awakened are spread out among the Black Land's villages, and the nomadic tribes which wander within and beyond its borders. Far from Re's influence yet untouched by the call of Duat, they seek the favor of the small gods of Neter-Khertet to ensure the prosperity of their own communities. (Fate)<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Singers of the False Heart:</b> When the Shuankhsen and the solar priesthood unleashed the Amkhata they created, they did not realize how much chaos they would wreak upon the Black Land in the decades that followed. Initiates of the Legacy combine their knowledge of Duat and Neter-Khertet to tame or destroy those which should not be. (Death)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Ba</u></b><br /> <br /> \u2022<br /> <br /> \u2022<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Word Bearers:</b> Like the Cryptologos of later eras, this Kemetic Legacy demonstrates great skill in the use of High Speech in their magic. They serve as translators for the Great House and the Weret-Hekau, and are often called upon to ensure the truth behind the words of foreign dignitaries. (Prime)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Ka</u></b><br /> <br /> \u2022<br /> <br /> \u2022<br /> <br /> \u2022<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Ren</u></b><br /> <br /> \u2022<br /> <br /> \u2022<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>The Unspoken:</b> Though feared for dark practices, most members of the Legacy only use their gifts on sorcerers who have fully rejected the Law. They are called upon by the Weret-Hekau to sunder the souls of such heretics, yet forever consign their own to Ammut through carrying out such acts. (Death)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Sheut</u></b><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Eyes of Ma'at:</b> Sorcerers who refined their magic to the task of stripping away Sekhem, this Legacy would form late into the war between the three alliances. After the battle at Nekhen-Nekheb, they continue to grow in numbers and prominence as they scour the kingdom for Deathless and Lifeless who chose to remain rather than scatter to the four winds. (Fate)<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Forge Masters:</b> Paying homage to the god, Ptah, the sorcerers of the Legacy work rituals which enchant and imbue items into potent vessels of magic. Some of their works are sought by Hemka of other sects, but most are enshrined within their reliquary at their patron's temple in Inbu-Hedj. (Prime)<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Stone Scribes:</b> In studying the mysteries of a departed soul's Ren, these Awakened sekhau invoke them alongside their utterances to perceive their mark on the Scroll of Ages. Some of these deceased are erased from the Scroll, their names stricken by the Scribes so that they do not harm the future with poisonous influence. (Time)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T23:31:38-07:00","id":909886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=906041#post906041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.madote.com/2010/03/land-of-punt-is-eritrea.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjtYsjCRvJ3aKmKLzfKtJ2_hqvtGfm0E6CVpHSb2PylXFfyVQ2K0CqVSWExwU98StnUQy22vVDIf59y3mwTbrjGk2ZyLrUNem5v3RZp27GMtskVLtndZy4aWoBa5V38S448GRPH-FCpIIw/w1200-h630-p-k-no-nu/Punt+people+2.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.madote.com/2010/03/land-of-punt-is-eritrea.html\" target=\"_blank\"> The Land of Punt is Eritrea </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.madote.com/2010/03/land-of-punt-is-eritrea.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.madote.com/2010/03/land-of-punt-is-eritrea.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Eritrean News and Views </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Might be relevant for your stuff on the Land of Punt. But that said, where did you place it as being located at when you were conceiving the Mumvuri?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really sure it is really relevant- while the most popular opinion is that Punt is found in East Africa (specifically, the Horn of Africa), the CofD seem to have chose a less accepted interpretation, placing it in Southern Africa to tie it with the Mutapa Kingdom of the great Zimbabwe. As such, most of the inspiration used for the Mumvuri came from those cultures, especially the Shona.<br /> <br /> Still, if that is truly the case, there should be some explanation for all the archaeological discoveries of that time in that region, so there is more than enough place to develop a culture at the Horn of Africa for the setting.It may even be that the place was used as a port or harbor to make expeditions to Punt until it was named something like &quot;Little Punt&quot; or &quot;Gate to Punt&quot;, creating the confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T08:24:12-07:00","id":910814,"title":"","content":"To be added to the Per Henet GDoc.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>When we are power:</b> The dead must live apart from the living. That is the Law, and we honor it as we walk beneath Khonsu's light. To do otherwise provokes the Devourer, and what's left of our souls are forfeit to her on our final descent to Duat. In Waset and most other cities in Ta-Sheema, the House of Repose rule and guide the Hungry Dead. We dedicate our Requiem in service to the gods, and remind our people of their place in the Black Land.<br /> <br /> <b>When we are in trouble:</b> It seldom happens. But when the Per Henet wanes in power, we have greater reason to stand united. The Cults of Sutek and Shezmu sow only Chaos wherever they reign. And foreign Kindred from lands beyond worsen that discord by spreading their ways. This cannot stand. As the righteous of Ma'at among the Damned, it is our duty to impose Order over Chaos, wherever it may arise.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, seeing as the Usiri are associated with Azar, I was thinking of having the Per Henet's greatest holdings be at Abdju instead of Inbu-Hedj. Thematically, it's very appropriate. The Hill of Relics <i>was</i> a traditional burial place for Kemet's first kings, and - coupled with their priesthood's reverence for the dead - the House of Repose would have had a perfect place to hold court for all the Hungry Dead in the Black Land.<br /> <br /> Of course, seeing as these are Kindred we're talking about, I imagine the &quot;old guard&quot; at Abdju would have been at odds with those of their kind who made Inbu-Hedj their home. This latter group would have probably been garnering more influence due to living close to the Great House, not to mention Abdju falls in prominence over the years due to the rise of Re's solar priests (and those of Nebthet).<br /> <br /> And then all the crazy stuff that went down in the First Turn would screw everything up.<br /> <br /> But anyway. Back on topic. What do you guys think? Should the Usiri Bloodline emerge as a result of Arisen rule at Abju? And would the Anubi Bloodline also be present here, seeing as Sothis Ascends explicitly mentions their namesake in the Abdju write-up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T12:46:20-07:00","id":911052,"title":"","content":"The Usiri emerging from the Arisen ruling as god-kings of Abdju seems quite likely, <i>especially </i>given their connections to Azar and their purpose of protecting and guiding Kindred in Torpor. They could easily have done so with the intention of protecting Deathless masters in Duat as well, and in time shaping their perceptions of the living world.<br /> <br /> I'm liking more of what's coming out of the Per Henet now, since the idea has had time to stew and become a bit more clear. In regards to the Anubi, I think they'd likely emerge in the city of Zawty, better known by its Greek name of Lycopolis. The city was a cult centre for Anpu, and was also a place of worship for Wepwawet, so it's our most likely &quot;Uratha-central&quot; for First Turn Kemet as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:25:19-07:00","id":911094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=911052#post911052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Usiri emerging from the Arisen ruling as god-kings of Abdju seems quite likely, <i>especially </i>given their connections to Azar and their purpose of protecting and guiding Kindred in Torpor. They could easily have done so with the intention of protecting Deathless masters in Duat as well, and in time shaping their perceptions of the living world.<br /> <br /> I'm liking more of what's coming out of the Per Henet now, since the idea has had time to stew and become a bit more clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here. And hopefully, we can get more worked out for their Laws and Oaths. I've already refluffed a couple of Invictus Oaths amechra mad some time back (with his permission).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=911052#post911052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to the Anubi, I think they'd likely emerge in the city of Zawty, better known by its Greek name of Lycopolis. The city was a cult centre for Anpu, and was also a place of worship for Wepwawet, so it's our most likely &quot;Uratha-central&quot; for First Turn Kemet as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Duly noted. Anyway, here's a work-in-progress write-up that concerns Kindred politics in the Black Land.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Strife Among the Damned</u></b><br /> <br /> The Per Henet have courts throughout the Black Land. But the Hill of Relics remains the greatest seat of their society. Here, Mekhet and Ushabti from the 42 nomes regularly convene in assembly at the necropolis, to discuss matters of the Hungry Dead as a whole. These gatherings have dictated the policies of their kind since the days of the First Dynasty, when Narmer had united Upper and Lower Kemet into one kingdom.<br /> <br /> However, a schism gradually forms in the last days of the Fifth Dynasty. Having built up their influence for centuries, the Kindred of Inbu-Hedj have grown strong enough to challenge the authority of Abdju's elders. They clamor for the nomes to send representatives to their city, so that they may better shape the fate of the Black Land. By the time Unas ascended to the throne, these Hungry Dead have swayed their fellows in several nomes to their side, and thus hold assemblies of their own.<br /> <br /> It is this state of division that the Kindred are in at the onset of the First Sothic Turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:44:59-07:00","id":911113,"title":"","content":"Actually, I could think of another place where the Per Henet could convene. A place where the legacy of Imhotep would be well felt, a place that covers 10.5 km<sup>2</sup> of temples, tombs, and tunnels that would make the underground Necropolis of the Camarilla look like a desperate attempt to mirror the city above. A place where even back to the First Dynasty, Pharaohs felt a need to erect monuments. A place that was once the teaching field of Azar. A place where the Shan'iatu erected the Lord of the Horizon, their hermitage and arcane laboratory. A place the Deathless cannot, will never, truly remember and that drains Sekhem for unknown purposes. A place where the greatest of the Shan'iatu may have established his labyrinthian tomb.<br /> <br /> Saqqara. Necropolis of The City of White Walls. Grave of the Nameless Empire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:54:41-07:00","id":911120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=911113#post911113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I could think of another place where the Per Henet could convene. A place where the legacy of Imhotep would be well felt, a place that covers 10.5 km<sup>2</sup> of temples, tombs, and tunnels that would make the underground Necropolis of the Camarilla look like a desperate attempt to mirror the city above. A place where even back to the First Dynasty, Pharaohs felt a need to erect monuments. A place that was once the teaching field of Azar. A place where the Shan'iatu erected the Lord of the Horizon, their hermitage and arcane laboratory. A place the Deathless cannot, will never, truly remember and that drains Sekhem for unknown purposes. A place where the greatest of the Shan'iatu may have established his labyrinthian tomb.<br /> <br /> Saqqara. Necropolis of The City of White Walls. Grave of the Nameless Empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>As in Ankhtawy, the Land of the Two Horizons? The necropolis mentioned in the Inbu-Hedj entry of Sothis Ascends? Huh. That was actually my first idea, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19pettOSEIP7X6VjDx8pjjZ4LJyyCjLUuazTh3U80JDo/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">as currently written here</a>, and I think we can make that be where the new assembly formed by the Inbu-Hedj Kindred convenes, separate from the original assemblies held at Abdju. What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:02:45-07:00","id":911127,"title":"","content":"The very same. And that is an excellent idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:22:16-07:00","id":911140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=911127#post911127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The very same. And that is an excellent idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Made the revision to that section.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Hungry Dead:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Ankhtawy may not have been conceived as the resting place of the Kindred, but the Per Henet hold their second largest court within its confines. Led by elders of Inbu-Hedj, a faction of the House of Repose has renounced the authority of the assembly at Abdju, and works to influence the Great House from the shadows. Those who still convene beneath the the Hill of Relics see this growing movement as a threat, as Kindred from the other nomes come under its banner. </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T20:19:52-07:00","id":911412,"title":"","content":"Finished writing up this little sidebar section for Abdju.<br /> <br /> -=- <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 624px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Servants of the Foremost Westerner</u></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mortals were not the only followers of the cult that sprang up in the Hill of Relics. Many of Kemet's supernatural denizens also come to revere Khenti-Amentiu, and later Azar and the Arisen in the same manner as the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>remet</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Bound to the Nameless:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Many of the city\u2019s death priests are Bound to nameless </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>akh</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, souls whose </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Ren</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> was lost in Duat. Rather than fade into oblivion, though, these shades forge pacts with the living to survive. And in doing so, they grant their hosts mastery over the dead that inspires awe and fear among even the Awakened of the priesthood. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Meetings Beneath the Hill:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Since Narmer united the two lands, Kindred from all 42 nomes have met in council at the necropolis at Abdju. Their assemblies brought about the rise of the Per Henet, and laid down the laws which all Hungry Dead follow throughout their Requiems. With the schism caused by those at Inbu-Hedj, though, the House of Repose finds itself on the verge of a civil war at the onset of the Turn.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Those Great of Magic:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Abdju\u2019s sect of Weret-Hekau stand apart from their peers, as they hold custody of one of Kemet\u2019s greatest Mysteries. They sensed the magic bound within their city\u2019s sacred mummies, and their divination rituals hinted at the coming cosmic event which would animate them. When the Sothic Turn does arrive, many of these sorcerers pledge allegiance to the Arisen who come to rule their city..</span></span></td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T17:47:40-07:00","id":913112,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this was more applicable in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a>'s Sundered World Chronicles. But I'll put it here anyway, on the assumption that the Werewolf sects from the Sundered World still persist even after all this time. <hr /><br /> <b>The</b> <b>Loyal (Umfinthimma)</b> struggle to keep the memory of Pangaea alive in the centuries that followed the unthinkable. Urfarah is dead, and the ancestral home of the werewolves died with him. As the only ones among his descendants who remained faithful to the end, it is their sacred duty to bring together their scattered race. The world must be claimed by the Uratha as one people, and the kinslayers who tore down their paradise are to answer for their crime.<br /> <br /> <b>The Cull (Kazithaga)</b> continue to curb the spread of humanity, as they had when the Border Marches still stood. With Urfarah and Pangaea gone, though, their hunts are driven by both vengeance and a desperate attempt at preventing further damage on the symbolism of the world. Theirs is a losing battle, however. Mortals have prospered in the wake of the Sundering, and their numbers continue to grow despite their efforts. Faced with this fact, many find allies among the Loyal as the two sects' goals align with one another.<br /> <br /> <b>The Maw (Gathua) </b>fractured into smaller sects since the Sundering. They could not slay enough of their own kind to restore the Great Predator's soul. Many blamed themselves for his death, as they did not act fast enough to slow his decline. These werewolves eventually chose to end their lives, whether at their own hands or those of others. Some, however, come to believe that their sect's purpose must change. Urfarah may be gone, but the Uratha continue to live and grow in number. They must continue to hunt their own, regardless of whether or not it might somehow bring him back to life.<br /> <br /> <b>The Shepherds (Sahenhar) </b>weathered the worst of the aftershocks of Pangaea's destruction. And in the countless years that have passed, they have found a place amongst the ever growing herd of humanity. In spite of her rejection, some still use what little they have of the moon's power to bring about more of their kind. Others are more preoccupied fighting the Gudthubak over stewardship of mankind.<br /> <br /> <b>The Inheritors (Ifila) </b>still fight to fill the void left by the passing of the Great Wolf. They still believe that it was necessary to kill him. But with the Firstborn having fled deep into the Shadow, and the Warden Moon having taken back her blessings, many grow convinced that Urfarah's death was a terrible mistake. A large number of these Uratha end up gravitating to the ranks of the Loyal. Those who remain keep true to their sect's new goals as their packs delve into the Shadow in search of the Great Predator's first children.<br /> <br /> <b>The Devourers (Tesfurfarrahu) </b>fared poorly in the new world. Their efforts to devour Urfarah's soul amounted to nothing when the Sundering struck. Denied of their goal, and devoid of a purpose, many degenerate into savage creatures not unlike the First Pack. Some fell so far into their spiritual halves that they ended up slipping through the Gauntlet into the Shadow. Those that manage to balance their natures either redirect their attention to their fellow Uratha, or somehow convert to the other sects.<br /> <br /> <b>The Mourners (Athdursa) </b>have persisted over the last thousand years, but now exist as a shadow of what they were. Pangaea is gone, yet creatures of flesh and spirit still find ways to cross through the Gauntlet that rose wih Urfarah's final howl. Many of the sect have drifted into the ranks of the Inheritors, taking on their progenitor's duty of enforcing the divide between the two worlds. The few that remain, though, grow darker and more radical in their beliefs. The Great Predator's death <i>did</i> separate Flesh and Shadow, but it falls to them to finish the deed. To that end, they develop rites to strengthen the Gauntlet's influence in their territories, and some even go so far as to seek out the children of Spider and enlist their aid in achieving a common goal. These Mourners do not realize the consequences of their actions, and the other Uratha may be forced to turn their fangs and claws against them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T10:58:25-07:00","id":917439,"title":"","content":"To anyone who happens to have a copy of the Pack supplement, I'd like to hear how you'd handle reskinning the following Lodges to the setting of the First Turn....<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>The Temple of Apollo:</b> Naturally, a Lodge similar to this one would be an offshoot of Re's faith among the Uratha, As for whether its patron is the Sun Wolf, itself, or perhaps an actual Hellion that the Lodge members somehow earned the respect of, I'd like to hear what you guys think.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>The Lodge of Garm:</b> Seeing as they are also known as the &quot;Fangs of Upuaut&quot;, I think it's safe to say that this lodge would dominate in the Kemetic city of Zawty, which was the cult center for Upuaut as a member of the Egyptian Pantheon. Furthermore, I can definitely see them aligning with the Iunu-Waset Alliance, seeing as the Arisen and Shuankhsen are both gods that they could try to hunt down and kill.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>The </b><b>Kazithaga: </b>Possibly coming to be called the Lodge of Irkalla at some point between the Sundering and the First Sothic Turn, the Pack supplement has confirmed that they have the same Sacred Prey as the Iron Master. However, they believe that <i>Urfarah</i> can return if they cast countless human souls into the Underworld to balance the scales. Ideally for them, this would mean open war against all of humanity for the sake of reviving a dead god.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Eaters of the Dead:</b> Ravening Wolf is most likely still alive here. And seeing as the Lodge write-up mentioned that its founder ate her corpse, am I right to assume that she was perhaps a Firstborn who maintained her nature as a Pangaean? If so, perhaps the undead who felled her in the first place could be either the Shuankhsen or the Arisen. The latter might be more likely, seeing as the Su-Menent might have somehow used what knowledge they had to kill <i>Isim-Ur</i>, and channel the power of her remains to create a Lodge similar to the modern Eaters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 06-21-2016, 07:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T07:17:56-07:00","id":919694,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://mirrorofisis.freeyellow.com/id210.html\" target=\"_blank\">Just read this little article here</a>, and it's definitely prompted me to try my hand at making a write-up of Khmun (Djehuti's cult center) similar to that of the cities mentioned in Sothis Ascends. Expect me to post it soon.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Here we go. Still a work-in-progress, though. Critique and additions are appreciated. <hr /><br /> KHMUN, THE EIGHT-TOWN (HERMOPOLIS)<br /> One of the more prosperous cities in Kemet, Khmun is the capital of the 15th Upper nome and center of worship for not one but nine gods. Eight of them are the Tepi-Aui-Un, primordial divinities who bore witness to the birth of Re and all of creation. The ninth is Djehuti, whom the remet-en-kemet honor as the scribe of the gods and foremost assessor of Ma'at.<br /> <br /> ---=---<br /> The Eightfold Pantheon:<br /> - The eight deities of the Tepi-Aui-Un (or Ogdoad, as they will be more commonly known) are divided into four male-female pairs. Each represents the male and female aspects of one of the four concepts of primordial chaos. Together, they embodied the primal, fundamental state of the beginning.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Nu and Naunet - Water<br /> \u2022 Amun and Amaunet - Air<br /> \u2022 Kuk and Kauket - Darkness<br /> \u2022 Huh and Hauhet - Eternity<br /> ---=---<br /> <br /> Khmun is a great city matches only by Iunu and Waset. Like the former, it is a place of learning, with Djehuti's priests practicing the same sorcery as the solar priesthood. Some even claim that Khmun's magical tradition eclipses that of the Place of Pillars. Yet despite the rivalries between them, the magicians of both cities stand together as allies when Kemet is plunged into civil war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 06-23-2016, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T08:32:14-07:00","id":928161,"title":"","content":"A new addition to the Werewolf section in the form of a conversion for the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/928108-lodge-of-the-red-sands-2e-conversion#post928108\">Lodge of the Red Sands</a>. The Age of Azar-related section in the thread is a work-in-progress, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T22:32:12-07:00","id":937942,"title":"","content":"<b><u>The Lonely Watchers - Wardens of the Black Land</u></b><br /> <br /> From the boat people who navigate the Nile to the lonely watchers of the Red Desert, Kemet counts a number of Wardens among its Immortals. Tied to minor gods who dwell in Neter-Khertet, these men and women cannot travel far from the sites they are anchored to without risking the loss of their gifts. Nevertheless, their influence extends far through their dealings with the other shadow peoples, and it is said that the eldest among them may possess knowledge on the predynastic empire that the Black Land was once part of. This is often enough of a reason for occult scholars to seek them out.<br /> <br /> As it is in modern nights, Wardens of this era favor a life of solitude. Some gather cults around themselves to keep them company throughout succeeding generations. Others are fortunate enough to befriend another kind of Immortal like the Eternals or the Purified, or at least a long-lived supernatural such as a Beast or one of the Awakened. Most of the time, though, a Warden is alone. His immortality and the price it exacts ultimately push him away from his mortal loved ones. And most supernaturals who know him eventually move on for one reason or another. The only being that can truly be considered the Warden's constant companion is the god that rules over his sacred place. But even then, such a bond might be rather impersonal at times.<br /> <br /> In exchange for such a lonely existence, Wardens are empowered by their patrons to protect the locations they are anchored to. Those tied to the river could become one with its waters, and rose up to drown those who would seek to defile its sanctity as neutral ground. Similarly, immortal nomads in the Deshret could similarly turn into shifting columns of air, and move at blinding speeds to assail those unworthy to uncover the desert's secrets. Such powers give some of them the might of a Claimed, while still retaining much of the free will and individuality they had as mortals.<br /> <br /> Many of Kemet's shadow peoples cultivate ties with one Warden or another. Uratha and Weret-Hekau approach the boat people to seek an audience with the river gods of the Nile. And the Cult of Sutek counts among its allies Wardens of the Red Desert who keep them informed of anything in the dunes. Many of these Immortals were thus among the first beings to encounter the Deathless and Lifeless as they emerged with the coming of the Turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T06:33:18-08:00","id":1012545,"title":"","content":"I'm going to be picking up where I left off on this. And for starters, does anyone have ideas for terms I could use to refer to changelings? Especially in Kemet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T10:08:10-08:00","id":1012644,"title":"","content":"Wait, is this just an invite to work on the setting, or an invite to a campaign on the forums?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T16:32:09-08:00","id":1012861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1012644#post1012644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, is this just an invite to work on the setting, or an invite to a campaign on the forums?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just an invite to work on a fan setting, which is basically a homebrew crossover expansion on a chapter of Sothis Ascends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T18:00:12-08:00","id":1012899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1012861#post1012861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just an invite to work on a fan setting, which is basically a homebrew crossover expansion on a chapter of Sothis Ascends.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What's a Sothis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T18:47:42-08:00","id":1012913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1012899#post1012899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What's a Sothis?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the Egyptian name for the star, Sopdet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T23:53:48-08:00","id":1013039,"title":"","content":"To add to thr Seats of the Gods doc as a sidebar for Per-Wadjet. And one additional point for Nekhen and Nekheb's.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Poison of Vision:</b> As the oracles of Lower Kemet, the Cult of Wadjet commands a great deal of influence, and this has only been reinforced since Khenut was made Unas' second wife. They have seen that Khenut's child will birth next line of kings, and thus work to ensure that mother and child live through the chaos engulfing the Black Land.<br /> <br /> <b>Lake of Dreams:</b> Of all the people who returned from the Sea of Reeds, those of Per-Wadjet are perhaps the most prosperous. These fae beings have built a city which mirrors Per-Wadjet in grandeur, and their courts enjoy access not only to a successful Market, but also a cornucopia of enchanted fruits grown in fertile soil.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Foresight of the Mothers:</b> Though they continue to give their services to the Great House, the Cult of Nekhbet holds no real loyalty to Unas.Their divinations have exposed to them the truth of the mad king, and that his actions threaten to drown Kemet in a storm of chaos and destruction. Armed with this knowledge, the Mothers secretly plot to avert the coming crisis before it is too late.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 12-06-2016, 03:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T16:34:33-07:00","id":1204732,"title":"","content":"Dark Eras 2 should have some more information we can use for the project; at the very least the Beast and Promethean sections aren't represented here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T16:39:48-07:00","id":1204735,"title":"","content":"Has anything been done for Beast, yet, or is that not a gameline this Dark Era focuses on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T21:29:19-07:00","id":1204786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1204732#post1204732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dark Eras 2 should have some more information we can use for the project; at the very least the Beast and Promethean sections aren't represented here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would definitely like more material to work with. Though for Prometheans, I think the only lineages that would make sense in this setting are Unfleshed, Ulgans (perhaps reskinned for use with Egyptian concepts of the soul) and Osirans (much later in the timeline, for obvious reasons.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1204735#post1204735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anything been done for Beast, yet, or is that not a gameline this Dark Era focuses on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I have been meaning to add a dedicated section for Beasts, seeing as Age of Azar expands upon the Cannibal Hymn chapter of Sothis Ascends. That said, there are some bits and pieces I've added in a few of the docs I've posted.<br /> <br /> On a related note, it'd be really nice to get my hands on the Beast Player's Guide. The content mentioned in the preview could be useful in fleshing out more, especially those Obascus Rites I've been hearing about. Maybe someone could think up ideas for mixing them with Sekhem Sorcery?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T03:11:30-07:00","id":1204822,"title":"","content":"Obascus Rites rely on a connection to the Dark Mother in several cases and certainly draw upon the Astral realm in all cases. Not for general use, as only one of the Begotten or their Heralds can perform them. They can also include much more...large scale effects, like say, placing an Environmental Tilt/Lair Trait on a city.<br /> <br /> The cross over potential between that and Sekhem Sorcery lies more in what happens when one is mistaken for the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T07:16:34-07:00","id":1204854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1204822#post1204822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obascus Rites rely on a connection to the Dark Mother in several cases and certainly draw upon the Astral realm in all cases. Not for general use, as only one of the Begotten or their Heralds can perform them. They can also include much more...large scale effects, like say, placing an Environmental Tilt/Lair Trait on a city.<br /> <br /> The cross over potential between that and Sekhem Sorcery lies more in what happens when one is mistaken for the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm starting to get that impression too. But the fact that these Rites can potentially impose large scale effects to a city would certainly make them fit with the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T07:42:59-07:00","id":1204860,"title":"","content":"Not disagreeing. Just noting that they work a little difference.<br /> <br /> Personally I'm still trying work out how the 4 active forms of alchemy in Kemet.<ul><li>(Sekhem/Relic) Alchemy [Mummy]</li> <li>(Pyros) Alchemy [from Promethean]</li> <li>(Surpenal) Alchemy (Mage)*</li> <li>(Toxic) Alchemy [Hunter; Ascending Ones Endowment, Egyptian cult]</li> </ul><br /> <br /> *Technically possible for many people as of Signs of Sorcery, as you just need cross Twilight or related worlds (such as the Shadow or the Underworld). So Sorcerers can do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T08:36:53-07:00","id":1204872,"title":"","content":"I think it\u2019d be cool, figuring out what an Apex in this ancient era would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T09:39:54-07:00","id":1204887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1204872#post1204872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it\u2019d be cool, figuring out what an Apex in this ancient era would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bronze or early Iron Age warlords? Local demons (small d, for the regional bugaboo)? Religious leaders ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T09:45:26-07:00","id":1204889,"title":"","content":"Hmmm...a Slaughterer Apex? OUCH. Or maybe a Shuankhsen? A Shuankhsen Apex would be <i>terrifying</i>, though I wonder what his or her or its Apex Hive Trait would be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T09:52:54-07:00","id":1204891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1204889#post1204889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm...a Slaughterer Apex? OUCH. Or maybe a Shuankhsen? A Shuankhsen Apex would be <i>terrifying</i>, though I wonder what his or her or its Apex Hive Trait would be?</div> </div> </div> </div>HUNGRY. So Hungry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T11:01:43-07:00","id":1204915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1204891#post1204891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> HUNGRY. So Hungry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've just imagined a crushing sensation at the word hunger. So maybe a literal Crushing Trait?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T12:45:20-07:00","id":1204946,"title":"","content":"I imagine... corpses. Countless in number - they wash ashore, fill pits with their rot, cover the ground as a blanket, lie piled up into mounds. A few of them are former victims or bodies the Shuankhsen once wore. Most aren't. The one time the Apex got to see the Hive, the very sight caused some sort of psychotic breakdown. The Shuankhsen wouldn't explain why, but strangely enough, they seemed to want to. The Beasts wonder what could be so terrifying to silence an Apex and some consider finding out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T19:19:59-07:00","id":1205051,"title":"","content":"A thought occurred to me, so I thought I\u2019d toss it out and see what everyone thinks.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Promethean Osiris was a demiurge\u2019s attempt to reincarnate Azar on Earth once more? It obviously didn\u2019t go as planned, but it would certainly explain the discrepancy between Azar and Osiris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T20:31:51-07:00","id":1205074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1205051#post1205051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thought occurred to me, so I thought I\u2019d toss it out and see what everyone thinks.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Promethean Osiris was a demiurge\u2019s attempt to reincarnate Azar on Earth once more? It obviously didn\u2019t go as planned, but it would certainly explain the discrepancy between Azar and Osiris.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would definitely make sense. Of course, the first Nepri's creation might date back to a later point in the First Sothic Turn. At the latest, it could be after the Arisen Diaspora and Unas' reign.<br /> <br /> That said, is it possible that another Lineage with the phlegmatic humour and the element of water were ascendant in this time? One that died out just like the Prophets?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T22:57:48-07:00","id":1205105,"title":"","content":"Possible but unlikely and I can't think of any thematically appropriate myth right now.Honestly, it could be a recent attempt, sparked by old prophecies of the Sothic Turn to 'raise the dead'.<br /> <br /> Or maybe someone tried in the interval between turns. I'd rather have them as a playable option than not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T23:42:14-07:00","id":1205109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1205105#post1205105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possible but unlikely and I can't think of any thematically appropriate myth right now.Honestly, it could be a recent attempt, sparked by old prophecies of the Sothic Turn to 'raise the dead'.<br /> <br /> Or maybe someone tried in the interval between turns. I'd rather have them as a playable option than not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd second that. Still, the Osirans will probably be known under a different name seeing as Azar was a name that the Egyptians forgot until the god was reintroduced by the Arisen. That said, Amenti/Amentiu would make sense as an older name for the Lineage if they were around then.<br /> <br /> On a different note. In &quot;A Land of Many Gods - Mystery Cults of Kemet&quot;, I have a section for a Relic called the Hand of Thoth which has not been filled up yet. Does anyone have ideas on what it could provide a high proest of Djehuty?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-10-2018, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T04:03:04-07:00","id":1205132,"title":"","content":"I am less comfortable coming up with MtC Relics than I should love for my love of the gameline. The quick and dirty version I have ATM works like so:<ul><li><i>The Hand of Thoth (3 dot Text Relic)</i></li> <li><i>A repository of knowledge and secrets to reveal the Lifeless and Deathless who desecrate Ma'at</i></li> <li><i>Cost: 3 Willpower</i></li> <li><i>Effect: It may act as a sufficient source of research on it's own to study the Lifeless and Deathless, as well as their minion though limited to only what has ever been written down (ever, so far), as the knowledge is drawn from the scroll of ages. This does not translate the text. Furthermore it grants 9-again bonus to any rolls that may identify and/or expose the group/individuals studied for a number of days equal to the reader's Resolve. If it is attempted to be used on an invalid target, the curse still manifests.</i></li> <li><i>Curse: The subjects who have been studied are made aware that an enemy has studied them through magic, as well as the ability to identify this enemy on sight. Furthermore the reader gains the Paranoid condition and may not begin to resolve it until the reader is no longer under the blessing. (9 again). </i></li> </ul><br /> This may be way off balance and obviously violates Memory.<br /> <br /> Back to the thing I feel more confident about, I found this place: <a href=\"http://medu.ipetisut.com/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://medu.ipetisut.com/index.php</a><br /> Not sure how useful it is but it an be mined.<br /> <br /> For example, <u>mytpune </u>means from. So Osirans might be called mytpune Azar.<br /> <br /> Though if the terminology does change, we may get some info from DE2.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T05:14:07-07:00","id":1205143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1205132#post1205132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am less comfortable coming up with MtC Relics than I should love for my love of the gameline. The quick and dirty version I have ATM works like so:</div> </div> </div> </div>This is still something I can work with. Thanks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T07:15:07-07:00","id":1205185,"title":"","content":"If you don't mind me asking, what are the current ideas on the gamelines that don't have (and won't receive anytime soon) official material for the era/region?<ul><li>Geists could be perceived as Akhs and Sin-Eaters as 'mini' pharaohs (houses for these 'honoured dead) but the concept is not only heretical but arguably anachronistic (since the akhs moving outside their tomb is apparently from the 12th Dynasty; though if the Bound was the 'tomb'...).</li> <li>The Unchained and the God-Machine represent something interesting here; Irem's legacy is mostly Sekhem Sorcery and Neithian Infrastructure which both feel like <i>competing influences </i>to the Infrastructure. Combined with the little nugget in the Giants of the Earth Shard (DSG), I get the feeling the Machine isn't very strong here and is attempting to lessen the forces I said were competing with it.</li> <li>Changeling is a game with great potential. I don't know how we should bring it over.</li> <li>Deviant does not exist yet, but it should get a spot somewhere. I'd likely play up the 'broken soul' angle, since that nugget of information is something more interesting when we know which part is broken and what effect it might have. (Scars might be considered linked to different parts, rightly or wrongly)</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":".  saw an auto-correct typo 7 years later 08-20-2023, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T08:55:20-07:00","id":1205232,"title":"","content":"Plus, what were the Deceived doing, during the First Sothic Turn? Did the shu tutor <i>them</i>, too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 04-10-2018, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T08:57:41-07:00","id":1205236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1205185#post1205185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't mind me asking, what are the current ideas on the gamelines that don't have (and won't receive anytime soon) official material for the era/region?<ul><li>Geists could be perceived as Akhs and Sin-Waters as 'mini' pharaohs (houses for these 'honoured dead) but the concept is not only heretical but arguably anachronistic (since the akhs moving outside their tomb is apparently from the 12th Dynasty; though if the Bound was the 'tomb'...).</li> <li>The Unchained and the God-Machine represent something interesting here; Irem's legacy is mostly Sekhem Sorcery and Neithian Infrastructure which both feel like <i>competing influences </i>to the Infrastructure. Combined with the little nugget in the Giants of the Earth Shard (DSG), I get the feeling the Machine isn't very strong here and is attempting to lessen the forces I said were competing with it.</li> <li>Changeling is a game with great potential . I don't know we should bring it over.</li> <li>Deviant does not exist yet, but it should get a spot somewhere. I'd likely play up the 'broken soul' angle, since that nugget of infomation is something more interesting when we know which part is broken and what effect it might have. (Scars might be considered linked to different parts, rightly or wrongly)</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>* The idea of Geists being akh was something I already wrote down in one of the docs for Age of Azar (Seats of the Gods - Cities of the Black Land). And it certainly would be nice to have some 2E mechanics to use as a basis.<br /> <br /> * The Unchained and God-Machine are a very weak presence alright. And that's what makes it so tricky for me to write them into the setting. The best I can probably do are a few footnotes here and there.<br /> <br /> * It'll be nice to have a set of changeling courts based on the flood cycle put together. It would be even better if other possible court systems can be made for Old Kingdom Egypt.<br /> <br /> * I got no comment for Deviant, but you are right that linking it with the Egyptian concept of the soul would be interesting to explore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T10:05:50-07:00","id":1205270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1205236#post1205236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* The Unchained and God-Machine are a very weak presence alright. And that's what makes it so tricky for me to write them into the setting. The best I can probably do are a few footnotes here and there.</div> </div> </div> </div>When the Machine doesn't have a strong presence, it just works more indirect and covertly. Manipulate this cultist here. Move this around for low-level Infrastructure development there. Any Angels are likely to be low-key. Demons would be sparse, but more likely to be worked with. When they aren't forming their own cults for support. Or even when they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T10:53:28-07:00","id":1205290,"title":"","content":"For demons, you could write it as demons fleeing there from far away specifically because so little GM influence is there. Also demons fight enroaching God-Machine Infrastructure into Egypt?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T11:24:36-07:00","id":1205307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1205290#post1205290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For demons, you could write it as demons fleeing there from far away specifically because so little GM influence is there. Also demons fight enroaching God-Machine Infrastructure into Egypt?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could also focus on what Infrastructure the God-Machine <i>does</i> have in the area, and how Demon's react to it. Especially since civilizations are just developing in much of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-10-2018, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T13:00:56-07:00","id":1205342,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Purified were a quasi-successful attempt to recreate the Spell of Rebirth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T05:04:08-07:00","id":1205539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1205232#post1205232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, what were the Deceived doing, during the First Sothic Turn? Did the shu tutor <i>them</i>, too?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine they did. Plus, the Utterances are name-based magic, so I can imagine the the Deceived (or rather their temakh) might have fervently hunted for them even at the start of the First Turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T05:50:13-07:00","id":1205552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1205290#post1205290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For demons, you could write it as demons fleeing there from far away specifically because so little GM influence is there. Also demons fight enroaching God-Machine Infrastructure into Egypt?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1205307#post1205307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also focus on what Infrastructure the God-Machine <i>does</i> have in the area, and how Demon's react to it. Especially since civilizations are just developing in much of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both are good points to work with. And it would also be easy to write out the Unchained in the context of them being outsiders and foreigners. The Cult of Sutek might even be considered a potential ally, seeing as GMC Angels would be very likely foes in their Vigil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T15:19:16-07:00","id":1205779,"title":"","content":"You know, some of the gods could be impersonated by various supernatural creatures. A werecrocodile Nahual pretending to be either Sobek, or an avatar of Sobek, and so on. Maybe some mages symbolically \u2018donning\u2019 a god\u2019s identity for magical purposes? And so on and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T16:16:37-07:00","id":1205809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1205779#post1205779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, some of the gods could be impersonated by various supernatural creatures. A werecrocodile Nahual pretending to be either Sobek, or an avatar of Sobek, and so on. Maybe some mages symbolically \u2018donning\u2019 a god\u2019s identity for magical purposes? And so on and so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there may well be a mention of this in DE2, with the Begotten claiming to be the gods or their hosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T16:54:07-07:00","id":1205825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1205809#post1205809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there may well be a mention of this in DE2, with the Begotten claiming to be the gods or their hosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Typhonic beast Inguma, claiming to be Set! Set was the god of outsiders, after all, how more \u2018fear of the other\u2019 could you get than <i>that</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T02:36:31-07:00","id":1206352,"title":"","content":"Added some of the crossover material from Princes of the Conquered Land (Dark Eras Companion) to the following doc on the hub.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Kz9W6ChdGnU8tV21Q-UgoRjWS_CrzC1D9ThJuDskBZY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Kz9W6ChdGnU8tV21Q-UgoRjWS_CrzC1D9ThJuDskBZY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Kz9W6ChdGnU8tV21Q-UgoRjWS_CrzC1D9ThJuDskBZY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Kz9W6ChdGnU8tV21Q-UgoRjWS_CrzC1D9ThJuDskBZY/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I've also added some bits for Mage characters who dabble in Sekhem sorcery (via the Ritual Sorcerer Merit). If any of you guys have any additions, feel free to suggest them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T10:47:24-07:00","id":1206523,"title":"","content":"Cross-posted this in my Thothite Homebrew since I think that bloodline is due for a redo. I might end up taking some inspiration from the Sefen-Haqr bloodline in the Requiem Homebrew Hub.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Bloodline Gift: Se-Akh</u></b><br /> Referring to a Kemetic ritual that unified the Ba and Ka to reanimate a person\u2019s Akh, the term is instead used by the Akhtet to the higher awareness gained upon realizing their heritage. The gift of Se-Akh confers three benefits to the Thothites.<br /> <br /> The first grants them an Unseen Sense to those empowered by Sekhem. With training, they can intuitively recognize Arisen or the Lifeless upon perceiving them directly in person, and can also detect the presence of Iremite relics. Furthermore, whenever the Thothite uses Auspex on a relic or one of the Deathless or Lifeless, he gains a number of free insights equal to half his Blood Potency (rounded up).<br /> <br /> The second is access to magic barred to undead and Undying alike. A Thothite can purchase the Ritual Sorcerer and Sorcerous Knowledge Merits, and can perform both Closed Rites and most Open Rites. This is attributed to the occult knowledge imbued into them by Thoth, though those who study it must still meet its requirements.<br /> <br /> The third benefit builds upon the second, for it allows the Thothites to focus Sekhem in ways only the Arisen can normally do - the magic of the Utterances. A Thothite can purchase Utterance Tiers as if they were Devotions, and has an effective Sekhem rating equal to half their Blood Potency, rounded up, for the purpose of both determining his maximum Utterance level and the number of participants that can be involved in a Unison tier's casting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T01:18:10-07:00","id":1206815,"title":"","content":"Tentative revision to FallenEco's Hand of Thoth writeup.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Hand of Thoth</u> (3-dot Text Relic)</b><br /> - A repository of knowledge and secrets, this Relic takes the form of a scroll fashioned from silver leaf and typically kept in a container displaying the Wedjat. The scroll itself is blank, but quickly becomes inscribed with luminescent script once used.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3 Willpower<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The Hand may act as a sufficient source of research on it's own to study even the most obscure of beings, as the knowledge is drawn from the Scroll of Ages. The text also translates itself automatically to the reader, and it can appear in cuneiform to a Sumerian reader while still showing hieroglyphics to an Egyptian.<br /> <br /> Reading from the scroll grants the 9-again quality to any rolls that may identify and/or expose the group or individuals studied for a number of days equal to the reader's Resolve.<br /> <br /> <b>Curse:</b> The subjects who have been studied are made aware that an enemy has learned something of them through magic, and also gain the 9-again quality on rolls to track and to identify this enemy. Furthermore, the reader suffers from the Obsession Condition related to those he studied with the Relic for the duration of its effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T07:25:48-07:00","id":1206875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1206523#post1206523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b><u>Bloodline Gift: Se-Akh</u></b><br /> --snip--<br /> The second is access to magic barred to undead and Undying alike. A Thothite can purchase the Ritual Sorcerer and Sorcerous Knowledge Merits, and can perform both Closed Rites and most Open Rites. This is attributed to the occult knowledge imbued into them by Thoth, though those who study it must still meet its requirements.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Sekhem) Ritual Sorcery is explicitly off limits to Vampires, Sin-Eaters, Arisen and others with an imbalance of Life and Death. This is a sticking point for me. Perhaps give them a bonus supernatural merit instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T09:17:25-07:00","id":1206908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1206875#post1206875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Sekhem) Ritual Sorcery is explicitly off limits to Vampires, Sin-Eaters, Arisen and others with an imbalance of Life and Death. This is a sticking point for me. Perhaps give them a bonus supernatural merit instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any suggestions for it? I'm open to any Merits that would be apt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T09:44:21-07:00","id":1206920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1206908#post1206908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any suggestions for it? I'm open to any Merits that would be apt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a Merit, but I think the Stolen Pillars Numina might be appropriate.<br /> <br /> EDIT: What with the <i>vampirism</i> inherent in stealing spiritual energy from other beings. <i>And</i> it would solve the problem of where they would get Pillar Points from to empower various Mummy tricks (like Relics and Utterances).<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: I just reread and it doesn't grant any actual Pillar Points (oddly). Still, it seems fitting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-14-2018, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T10:11:17-07:00","id":1206932,"title":"","content":"Allow them to steal Pillar ala the Shuankhsen? Their Bloodline Gift could be the ability to steal Pillars (and expend them every night along with Vitae?) And use Sekhem Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T18:16:23-07:00","id":1207100,"title":"","content":"Silly question; are we going to revisit how Hunter Endowments for Era Conspiracies work with an eye toward the proposed method for <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/revising-endowments-hunter-the-vigil\" target=\"_blank\">2E</a>?<br /> I liked the new approach and felt it made Endowments more distinct from regular merits.<br /> <br /> Edit: On the subject of Hunters, the homebrew groups should be linked on the first page. I have a small list of the ones mentioned in the google doc and noticed some others that might be applicable.<br /> <br /> Listed in doc (Not including Ascending Ones)<ul><li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/634487-the-nibiru-conspiracy\">The Legacy of Gilgamesh</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/507852-the-temple-of-silence-cosnpiracy\">Seeds of the Named Flower</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/841192-followers-of-set-full-writeup\">Cult of Sutek</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/600502-maw-of-the-river-mummy-hunters\">Teeth of the Crocodile God</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/38053-dying-conspiracy-ebony-fangs\">The Fangs of Irkalla</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/584777-maagal-habaal-vehaashera-dark-eras-book-of-judges\">The Silent Gods of Canaan</a></li> </ul><br /> New additions?<ul><li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1011415-hrt-isfet-strains-of-cursed-blood-north-africa\">Hrt Isfet</a></li> </ul><br /> I must admit it seems that the Serpent Blooded arose during this time, but we could tweak it so that the first were created by Apep to serve as 'mini-Heralds' before the group was reorganized (with help) into the binding force that now keeps it trapped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 04-14-2018, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T21:50:01-07:00","id":1207159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1207100#post1207100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silly question; are we going to revisit how Hunter Endowments for Era Conspiracies work with an eye toward the proposed method for <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://theonyxpath.com/revising-endowments-hunter-the-vigil&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">2E</a>?<br /> I liked the new approach and felt it made Endowments more distinct from regular merits.<br /> <br /> I must admit it seems that the Serpent Blooded arose during this time, but we could tweak it so that the first were created by Apep to serve as 'mini-Heralds' before the group was reorganized (with help) into the binding force that now keeps it trapped.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking we ought to wait until the official 2E rules come out before revising the Endowment system. But if anyone wants to take a stab at it now, feel free to do so.<br /> <br /> As for the Hrt Isfet, their predecessors were probably either split between full Heralds and (more commonly) Claimed. If we go with making the full First Turn (not just the Cannibal Hymn) as the setting, then we can work out the Serpent-Blooded during the first days of their existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T11:23:41-07:00","id":1207719,"title":"","content":"Does anyone happen to know of any material regarding the city of Khmun (Hermopolis) during the 5th Dynasty Era (aka the First Sothic Turn)? I might end up writing about it in a separate doc seeing as is Thoth's foremost city and the Thothite bloodline has been my latest focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T06:33:10-07:00","id":1209599,"title":"","content":"Can someone provide some commentary and critique on this conversion of the Aspect? It's very tricky for me to work out, but it's kinda relevant due to how other shapechangers are prominent in Kemet compared to werewolves.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Beast Magic</u> (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Select werebeasts pursue the arts of magic, employing arcane secrets and ominous tools to mimic the spells of human wizards. This is not without its dangers, though, and most ferals shun these strange arts because of how they limit their own primal potential. Nevertheless, those who do pursue it \u2014 cats, baboons, goats, foxes, cranes, spiders, frogs, ravens, even bison \u2014 are strongly attuned to the power granted, and consider the cost a fair trade. In human form, these creatures are often drawn to occult practices. And after the First Change, these practices come to fruition through the odd talent of Beast Magic.<br /> <br /> In game terms, this Aspect allows a werebeast to purchase and use mage spells from a specific Arcanum, and it can be purchased multiple times to expand their magical repertoire. Furthermore, they make use of the following rules. <br /> <br /> * A feral must spend a Willpower point to perform Creative Thaumaturgy with Beast Magic.<br /> <br /> * When performing a spell with Beast Magic, the character uses a dice pool of Primal Urge + Beast Magic.<br /> <br /> * A given spell always costs Essence equal to its dot rating (with a minimum of 1 point).<br /> <br /> * A feral can purchase rotes as Merits with a dot rating equal to their level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T06:47:54-07:00","id":1209601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1209599#post1209599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone provide some commentary and critique on this conversion of the Aspect? It's very tricky for me to work out, but it's kinda relevant due to how other shapechangers are prominent in Kemet compared to werewolves.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Beast Magic</u> (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Select werebeasts pursue the arts of magic, employing arcane secrets and ominous tools to mimic the spells of human wizards. This is not without its dangers, though, and most ferals shun these strange arts because of how they limit their own primal potential. Nevertheless, those who do pursue it \u2014 cats, baboons, goats, foxes, cranes, spiders, frogs, ravens, even bison \u2014 are strongly attuned to the power granted, and consider the cost a fair trade. In human form, these creatures are often drawn to occult practices. And after the First Change, these practices come to fruition through the odd talent of Beast Magic.<br /> <br /> In game terms, this Aspect allows a werebeast to purchase and use mage spells from a specific Arcanum, and it can be purchased multiple times to expand their magical repertoire. Furthermore, they make use of the following rules. <br /> <br /> * A feral must spend a Willpower point to perform Creative Thaumaturgy with Beast Magic.<br /> <br /> * When performing a spell with Beast Magic, the character uses a dice pool of Primal Urge + Beast Magic.<br /> <br /> * A given spell always costs Essence equal to its dot rating (with a minimum of 1 point).<br /> <br /> * A feral can purchase rotes as Merits with a dot rating equal to their level.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not sure giving them Arcana wholesale is a good idea... Maybe something like Proximi, where they buy spells separately?<br /> <br /> Wait, how did Pangaeans use Arcana again? Maybe there\u2019s something to mine from them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T07:02:15-07:00","id":1209607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1209599#post1209599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Beast Magic</u> (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Select werebeasts pursue the arts of magic, employing arcane secrets and ominous tools to mimic the spells of human wizards. This is not without its dangers, though, and most ferals shun these strange arts because of how they limit their own primal potential. Nevertheless, those who do pursue it \u2014 cats, baboons, goats, foxes, cranes, spiders, frogs, ravens, even bison \u2014 are strongly attuned to the power granted, and consider the cost a fair trade. In human form, these creatures are often drawn to occult practices. And after the First Change, these practices come to fruition through the odd talent of Beast Magic.<br /> <br /> In game terms, this Aspect allows a werebeast to purchase and use mage spells from a specific Arcanum, and it can be purchased multiple times to expand their magical repertoire. Furthermore, they make use of the following rules.<br /> <br /> * A feral must spend a Willpower point to perform Creative Thaumaturgy with Beast Magic.<br /> <br /> * When performing a spell with Beast Magic, the character uses a dice pool of Primal Urge + Beast Magic.<br /> <br /> * A given spell always costs Essence equal to its dot rating (with a minimum of 1 point).<br /> <br /> * A feral can purchase rotes as Merits with a dot rating equal to their level.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does the dot levels of the Merit do? Is it that you're supposed to buy this Merit for each Rote, or is it that dot rating of this Merit caps how advanced Rotes the werebeast can buy? (If the latter, what is the cost of Rotes? One XP per Rote like mages, or one XP per dot of the Rote like Proximi Blessings?) And when you say Rotes, do you mean something similar to Blessings rather than the ability to use a Mudra and/or apply Rote Action to casting the spell?<br /> <br /> Also, how many Reaches to they get, and how do they deal with Paradox?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T07:57:21-07:00","id":1209626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1209601#post1209601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not sure giving them Arcana wholesale is a good idea... Maybe something like Proximi, where they buy spells separately?<br /> <br /> Wait, how did Pangaeans use Arcana again? Maybe there\u2019s something to mine from them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm either thinking that they'd need to spend a Willpower point to do Creative Thaumaturgy of any kind, while learning a rote removes that.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, maybe removing Creative Thaumaturgy altogether could balance things out. As for the Merit, it's for each Rote, and I might end up going with the Proximi XP costs and mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T13:09:50-07:00","id":1209755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1209626#post1209626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I'm either thinking that they'd need to spend a Willpower point to do Creative Thaumaturgy of any kind, while learning a rote removes that.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, maybe removing Creative Thaumaturgy altogether could balance things out. As for the Merit, it's for each Rote, and I might end up going with the Proximi XP costs and mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not seeing why [Redacted from memory] should get Mage magic when they should be more similar to Werewolves. Any reason Wolf/Pack Rite access or Influences (as per Spirits or Horrors, depending on if Essence or Willpower is the fuel stat) wouldn't work? Influences are kinda like Arcana, but both more common/Blue Book/accessible and more category-limited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T13:18:50-07:00","id":1209756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1209755#post1209755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not seeing why [Redacted from memory] should get Mage magic when they should be more similar to Werewolves. Any reason Wolf/Pack Rite access or Influences (as per Spirits or Horrors, depending on if Essence or Willpower is the fuel stat) wouldn't work? Influences are kinda like Arcana, but both more common/Blue Book/accessible and more category-limited.</div> </div> </div> </div>So something more akin to Lodge Sorcery? Pack Rites and Rites exclusive to a specific type of shapechanger could work as well, and there is an Aspect that allows for the purchase of Numina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T15:45:24-07:00","id":1209795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1209756#post1209756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So something more akin to Lodge Sorcery? Pack Rites and Rites exclusive to a specific type of shapechanger could work as well, and there is an Aspect that allows for the purchase of Numina.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. It works better with the comparison to Werewolves, since both leverage the Spirit world/Shadow. It would make sense, that for &quot;animal magic&quot;, leveraging the powers of animal Spirits would make the most sense. Special Rites also allow for both greater variety of powers, as well as restricting them to thematic things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T04:22:19-08:00","id":1271413,"title":"","content":"I know that this project was sidelined in part in order to wait for the book to drop (and more Chronicle editions released) but there was a DE2 <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/chronicles-of-darkness-dark-eras-2/posts/2301240\" target=\"_blank\">Update released a while back that has some relevence.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T03:50:03-08:00","id":1276421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar?p=1271413#post1271413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that this project was sidelined in part in order to wait for the book to drop (and more Chronicle editions released) but there was a DE2 <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/chronicles-of-darkness-dark-eras-2/posts/2301240&amp;quot;]Update</a> released a while back that has some relevence.[/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div>OwO<br /> This is making me want to revisit and add to the content again. While this draft is chronologically set during the Middle Kingdom, I can see elements of this being referenced and integrated into the Age of Azar setting.<br /> <br /> That said, compared to the Mage and Vampire content, the Werewolf (and Shapechanger) section is a bit underdeveloped, so any suggestions based on this tidbit are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T04:16:44-08:00","id":1282270,"title":"","content":"Two of the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/profane-mysteries-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">Garm Lodge secrets reference the ancient Egyptian origins of the cult.</a> The Sand spirits with sacrifices and the secret First Tongue hieroglyphs sound like we might want to use them in this setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T22:14:59-07:00","id":1521010,"title":"","content":"Actually since someone brought this thread to my attention again, I feel the need to point out that the Garm Lodge implied it used to be &quot;courted by&quot; the Pure, if the Lodge wasn't actually part of the Pure in antiquity.<br /> <br /> In somewhat unnecessary news, I find the new website format less useful for reading the old blogposts so I am just going to post the relevant &quot;secrets&quot; here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris Allen - Profane Mysteries on Onyx Path</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Lodge of Garm: Mysteries of the God-Killers</b><br /> ...<ul><li>To repay loyal spirits of strife or destruction, Garm orders Lodge cells to stir up conflict amongst mortal communities. His wolf-servants of sand and hieroglyphs judge disobedient cultists harshly, but sometimes gift successful cells with fetish weapons wrought from wolf-teeth and bronze.</li> <li>The Lodge guards two secret forms of the written First Tongue, one a runic script and the other in hieroglyphs. The cult believes the runes and glyphs hold special power over wolf spirits and Uratha ancestor spirits. Garmir uses these sacred scripts to call and bind ancestral spirits of their enemies, denying the Pure their allies. Trapped spirits undergo terrible torments and inquisitions by the God-Killer\u2019s brood.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}